        defense: [E(.physical, 1, "Torn Tire", "A shredded front tire on {D}'s truck.")],
        role: "Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What did the gas station camera show?", "\"Two trucks revving at the exit and launching together onto the county road, side by side.\""), .direct("What did your reconstruction show?", "\"One truck traveling about 85 in a 45 zone before it left the road and went onto the shoulder.\""), .direct("Where did {V} come into this?", "\"{V} was setting up a roadside produce stand on the shoulder when the truck left the road and struck {V}.\""), .direct("What did the autopsy find?", "\"Fatal blunt injuries. {V} died at the scene from the force of the impact.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"Tire marks leaving the road, debris from the stand, and one truck at rest in a ditch with the driver still inside.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you at the scene?", "\"That a front tire blew out and the truck pulled hard to the right. {D} said the truck was not racing.\""), .cross("Did a tire fail on {D}'s truck?", "\"The tire was shredded after the crash. I cannot say whether it failed before or because of the impact.\""), .cross("Does the camera show both drivers racing?", "\"It shows both revving and launching together. It does not show the road after the first stretch.\""), .cross("Did you find the other truck?", "\"We identified it later. The other driver cooperated, and the camera confirms both trucks left together.\""), .cross("Was {D} impaired?", "\"No. {D} was sober. Testing showed no alcohol or drugs, and {D} stayed at the scene.\""), .cross("Was {D} wearing a seat belt?", "\"Yes, and {D} was injured in the crash. I do not doubt {D}'s distress at the scene.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Tire shop mechanic",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your work?", "\"I am a mechanic at a tire shop. I have mounted and inspected tires for many years and see failures often.\""), .direct("Did you inspect {D}'s truck tire before the crash?", "\"I looked at it a few weeks earlier. The front tire had a bulge on the sidewall, and it was overdue for replacement.\""), .direct("What does a bulge indicate?", "\"Internal damage to the tire. A bulge means the tire can fail suddenly without warning, especially at speed.\""), .direct("Did you tell {D} about it?", "\"Yes. I told {D} the tire needed to be replaced soon. {D} said {D.he} would come back and could not afford it that week.\""), .direct("What happens when a tire like that blows?", "\"The truck can pull hard to one side, and the driver can lose control in an instant, especially at speed.\""), .direct("Can a tire shred on impact?", "\"Yes. A hard impact can shred a tire. It is not always easy to tell what failed first.\""), .cross("Would a bulged tire be the only reason to lose control?", "\"No. Speed also matters, and a driver going fast has less time to correct.\""), .cross("Did you ever see the tire blow?", "\"No. I only inspected it earlier. I did not see the crash or the tire after.\""), .cross("Did you tell {D} not to drive on it?", "\"I told {D} to replace it soon. I did not say it was unsafe to drive.\""), .cross("Would a tire at 85 miles an hour be riskier?", "\"Yes. Higher speed puts more stress on a weak tire, and failure is more likely.\""), .cross("Is {D} a regular customer?", "\"Yes, for a few years. That does not change what I saw on the tire.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} raced a pickup and killed a roadside vendor.", "A blowout, not a race."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I will carry this.\"",
        truths: ("A group chat showed {DL} agreeing to race at the gas station.", "The tire had a recall for a tread separation."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you racing?", "\"No. I was not racing. I was on my way and the truck started pulling hard to the right.\""), .direct("What happened on the county road?", "\"The front tire went and the truck jerked right. I tried to hold it, but the truck left the road.\""), .direct("Did you rev at the gas station exit?", "\"I did. I revved the engine, and it was a stupid thing to do. The other driver revved too.\""), .direct("How fast were you going?", "\"Too fast. I was over the limit, and I cannot say it was safe. I am deeply sorry.\""), .direct("Did you know the tire was bad?", "\"The mechanic told me it needed to be replaced soon. I could not afford it that week, and I put it off.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about {V}?", "\"Terrible. {V} was only setting up a stand, and I will carry this for the rest of my life.\""), .cross("You revved your engine at the exit and launched with the other truck, didn't you?", "\"We pulled out at the same time. I did not agree to race, but I know what it looked like.\""), .cross("You were doing about 85 in a 45, weren't you?", "\"I was going too fast, and I do not dispute the number. It was a mistake.\""), .cross("The tire was shredded and the mechanic warned you, didn't the mechanic?", "\"The mechanic warned me about the bulge. I did not think it would fail that day.\""), .cross("You put off replacing a bulged tire, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Money was tight, and I told myself it would be fine. It was not.\""), .cross("A person died because of how you were driving, didn't they?", "\"A person died, and I was driving.\"")],
        openings: ("Two pickups revved at a gas station exit, launched together, and raced a county road. One left the road at about 85 in a 45 and killed {V}, who was setting up a produce stand. {D} drove that truck.", "A front tire with a known bulge failed, and the truck pulled hard to the right. {D} was not racing and tried to hold the truck. A blowout is a tragedy and not a street race."),
        closings: ("Two trucks launched together, 85 in a 45, and {V} dead on the shoulder. The tire was weak, but {D} chose the speed and chose to rev at that exit.", "A tire with a bulge, a truck that pulled right, and a driver who never meant to race. The State must prove {D} drove recklessly and not that the tire failed."),
        timeline: [(0, "7:30 a.m.: the gas station."), (0, "7:32 a.m.: the crash."), (0, "7:50 a.m.: medics."), (0, "8:15 a.m.: {V} is pronounced dead.")],
        identified: "A gas station camera.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "The stand fed a family of five.",
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let scaleAndBagsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.scaleAndBags",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Pocket Scale and Tiny Bags Found in Gym Bag After Motel Complaint", "Guest Says Items Were for a Spice Business"],
        law: "possParaphernalia",
        spec: "Knowingly possessed drug paraphernalia, a digital scale and small plastic bags, with intent to package a controlled substance, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...45,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Deputies answered a motel complaint about steady foot traffic on {DATE}. In a gym bag in {D}'s room they found a pocket scale with a white film and a box of tiny bags. No drugs were found. {DL} says {D.he} blends and sells spice mixes at farmers' markets.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Scale and Baggies", "A pocket scale with a white film and a box of tiny bags in a gym bag.", .search), E(.statement, 2, "Motel Clerk", "The clerk says visitors came and went all evening.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Market Permit", "A farmers' market vendor permit for spice blends.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What brought you to the motel room?", "\"A complaint about steady foot traffic. The clerk told us visitors had come and gone all evening.\""), .direct("What did you find in the room?", "\"In a gym bag, a pocket scale with a white film on it and a box of tiny bags.\""), .direct("Were any drugs found?", "\"No. We searched the room and the bag, and we found no drugs of any kind.\""), .direct("What else was in the bag?", "\"A vendor permit for farmers' markets and a few jars of dried herbs. It was in the same gym bag.\""), .direct("What did the motel clerk say?", "\"That visitors came and went all evening. The clerk did not describe anyone handing over anything.\""), .direct("What did you do with the scale?", "\"We took it for lab testing. The white film was sent to the lab, and I do not testify to results.\""), .cross("Is it a crime to own a pocket scale?", "\"No. Many people own pocket scales for cooking, crafts, or sales. A scale alone is not a crime.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone exchange money or items?", "\"No. I did not see a hand-to-hand sale, and no one admitted buying anything.\""), .cross("Did the permit match {D}?", "\"Yes. The vendor permit was in {D}'s name, and it listed spice mixes.\""), .cross("How many visitors were there?", "\"The clerk said several, but gave no number. I did not interview the visitors.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D} let us in, answered questions, and explained the scale and the bags right away.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} had packaging tools for drugs.", "A seller of spice blends."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I'll stay away from that crowd.\"",
        truths: ("The lab found cocaine residue on the scale.", "The film was powdered sugar and dried herbs, the lab reported."),
        defendant: [.direct("What do you do for work?", "\"I blend and sell spice mixes at farmers' markets. I rent stalls on weekends and sell dry rubs and seasoning blends.\""), .direct("What is the scale for?", "\"Weighing spices. I portion every mix by weight so each packet is the same, and I need a precise scale.\""), .direct("What was the white film on it?", "\"Powdered sugar from a cookie mix I was testing. Some of my blends use sugar, and it left a film.\""), .direct("What are the tiny bags for?", "\"Sample packets. I hand out tiny samples at the markets so customers can taste before they buy.\""), .direct("Who were the visitors?", "\"Friends and customers. A few came to pick up orders, and a few came to try new blends.\""), .direct("Why were you at a motel?", "\"I was between places and working a market in town. The room was cheap, and I used it to prep mixes.\""), .cross("You had a scale and a box of tiny bags in a motel room, didn't you?", "\"Yes. They were part of my spice business. I carry them everywhere I work.\""), .cross("Visitors came and went all evening, didn't they?", "\"Some came by, yes. I had orders to hand off and friends who wanted to try the blends.\""), .cross("A white film on a scale looks like drug residue, doesn't it?", "\"It could to someone who does not know. To me it was sugar and herbs, and I said so right away.\""), .cross("You were not selling spice at a motel at night, were you?", "\"I was prepping and handing off orders. I know how it looks, and I would have chosen a different place.\""), .cross("No drugs were found, correct?", "\"Correct. Nothing was found because I do not deal drugs, and I never have.\"")],
        openings: ("Deputies answered a motel complaint about steady foot traffic and found, in {D}'s gym bag, a pocket scale with a white film and a box of tiny bags. No drugs were found, and visitors had come and gone all evening.", "{D} blends and sells spice mixes at farmers' markets, with a vendor permit in the same bag. A scale, sample bags, and powdered sugar describe a baker, not a dealer."),
        closings: ("A scale with residue, a box of tiny bags, and a motel room with steady visitors all evening. Each piece alone may be explained, but together they describe a dealer's setup.", "No drugs, a vendor permit, spice jars, and a clerk who saw only visitors. The State cannot prove a sale from a scale and a box of sample bags."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: motel complaint."), (0, "9 p.m.: deputies knock."), (0, "9:20 p.m.: the bag is searched.")],
        identified: "A motel complaint and a room search.",
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure", "burdenOfProof"])

    static let bankNoteRobberyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.bankNoteRobbery",
        category: .robbery,
        headlines: ["Hooded Driver Sends Demand Note Through Credit Union Drive-Up Tube", "Gray Sedan Leads Deputies to Robbery Suspect"],
        law: "commonLawRobbery",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Took $1,800 in United States currency from the person and presence of {V}, a credit union teller, by putting {V.him} in fear, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 22...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A hooded driver in a gray sedan sent a note through the drive-up tube at a credit union on {DATE}: 'Everything in the drawer, now, I am armed.' {V}, the teller, sent $1,800 back. A plate reader tied the sedan to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} was at work when it happened.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Drive-Up Camera", "A hooded driver in a gray sedan sends a note and takes the cash."), E(.physical, 3, "Sedan and Hoodie", "A gray sedan registered to {D} and a matching hoodie at {D}'s home.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Time Clock", "{DL}'s punch at a warehouse at 10:02 a.m., six miles away.")],
        role: "Credit union teller",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a teller at the credit union. I work the drive-up window and handle cash drawers.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A hooded driver in a gray sedan sent a note through the tube that said everything in the drawer, now, I am armed.\""), .direct("How did you respond?", "\"I was terrified. I sent $1,800 back through the tube and pressed the alarm as soon as the car left.\""), .direct("What does the drive-up camera show?", "\"The gray sedan, the hooded driver, the note going in, and the cash being taken.\""), .direct("What did a plate reader show?", "\"It tied the sedan to {D}. The plate and vehicle match a gray sedan registered to {D}.\""), .direct("What was found at {DL}'s home?", "\"A matching hoodie, in a search of {D}'s home.\""), .direct("What did you do after you read the note that came through the tube?", "\"I sent $1,800 back through the tube and pressed the silent alarm. I was terrified because the note said the driver was armed, and I could not see a weapon.\""), .cross("Did you see the driver's face?", "\"No. The driver wore a hood and sunglasses. I could not identify anyone.\""), .cross("Did you see the note's handwriting?", "\"Yes, but I do not know whose it was. It was block lettering.\""), .cross("Is a gray sedan an uncommon car?", "\"No. Many gray sedans exist. The plate reader is what tied this one to {D}.\""), .cross("Could someone else have used {D}'s sedan?", "\"I do not know who had access to it. I only know whose name it is registered to.\""), .cross("Did anyone place {DL} at the credit union?", "\"No. Nobody has identified {D} as the driver.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Warehouse supervisor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a warehouse supervisor. I manage the dock crew and the time clock.\""), .direct("Was {DL} at work that morning?", "\"Yes. {D}'s punch shows 10:02 a.m. at the warehouse.\""), .direct("How far is the warehouse from the credit union?", "\"About six miles. It would take fifteen minutes or so.\""), .direct("What did {DL} do after clocking in?", "\"Went to the dock and loaded a truck. I saw {D} there.\""), .direct("What does the dock camera show?", "\"{D} loading a truck at 10:10 a.m. It matches what I remember.\""), .direct("What is {DL} like at work?", "\"Reliable and steady. I have never had a problem.\""), .direct("Walk us through how you saw {D} at the warehouse that morning.", "\"I saw {D} on the dock loading a truck at about 10:10. I remember it clearly, because the truck was late and I was watching the schedule.\""), .direct("How does the time clock work at the warehouse?", "\"Each worker has a badge that is swiped at the clock. It records the time, but it does not confirm that the person holding the badge is the worker.\""), .direct("What do you know about {D}'s coworkers and borrowed badges?", "\"I know it has happened. Workers sometimes punch in for each other, which is against the rules, and I cannot say whether it happened on that morning.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} punch in?", "\"No. I saw the record.\""), .cross("Can a badge be used by someone else?", "\"It can be borrowed. I would have to check the records.\""), .cross("Where was {DL} at 9:50?", "\"I do not know. I was on the dock with others.\""), .cross("Was the robbery before 10:02?", "\"I do not know the exact time.\""), .cross("Did anyone else punch in that morning?", "\"I do not recall.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sent a note through a tube and took the cash.", "A worker on the clock miles away."),
        allocution: "\"I was out of options. I'm sorry I scared you.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a coworker punch in with a borrowed badge that morning.", "The dock camera showed {DL} loading a truck at 10:10 a.m."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where were you that morning?", "\"At my warehouse job, working. I clocked in before the robbery and was on the dock by ten.\""), .direct("Whose car was the sedan?", "\"Mine. It is a gray sedan registered to me, but I was not driving it that morning.\""), .direct("Who had access to it?", "\"Several people. I lend it to friends sometimes, and the keys hang near my door.\""), .direct("What about the hoodie?", "\"A common gray hoodie. I own several, and so do half the people I know.\""), .direct("Did you rob the credit union?", "\"No. I have never done anything like that. I was at work.\""), .direct("What do you want people to know?", "\"That I was on the clock. A time card does not lie.\""), .direct("What does the time clock show about your punch that morning?", "\"It shows I punched in at 10:02 at the warehouse, six miles away. A coworker may have punched in for me with a borrowed badge, and I should have told the truth about that at first.\""), .cross("Your punch at 10:02 does not cover 9:50, does it?", "\"It shows I was at work soon after. I did not rob anyone.\""), .cross("A coworker could have punched you in, couldn't they?", "\"I do not know of anyone who did.\""), .cross("The sedan was yours, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, it is mine.\""), .cross("The hoodie was found in your home, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, in my closet where it always is.\""), .cross("You live six miles from the credit union, don't you?", "\"Near enough, yes. That proves nothing.\"")],
        openings: ("A hooded driver in a gray sedan sent a note through a credit union drive-up tube demanding cash, claiming to be armed. A plate reader tied the sedan to {D}, and a matching hoodie was at {D}'s home. The State will show the camera and the search.", "A time clock at a warehouse six miles away shows {D} at work minutes after the robbery. The supervisor will tell you where {D} was."),
        closings: ("A gray sedan registered to {D}, a matching hoodie, and $1,800 sent back through the tube. A plate reader tied the car to {D}, and a borrowed badge accounts for the time clock.", "A time clock at a warehouse six miles away and a dock camera showing {D} loading a truck minutes after the robbery. The State has not proved that {D} was the driver in the hood."),
        timeline: [(0, "10:08 a.m.: the note is sent."), (0, "10:09 a.m.: the silent alarm."), (0, "11:40 a.m.: a plate reader hits."), (1, "Search of {DL}'s home.")],
        identified: "A plate reader and a registered sedan.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mitigating: ["The defendant has accepted responsibility"],
        impact: "I still hear the tube whoosh when I close my eyes.",
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let partyGrabV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.partyGrab",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Restaurant Lot Camera Shows Boyfriend Grab and Shove Woman Into Car", "Valet Calls Deputies After Argument Turns Physical"],
        law: "assaultFemale",
        spec: "Assaulted {V}, a female, being a male over eighteen years of age, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After dinner on {DATE}, {D} grabbed {V}, {D.his} girlfriend, by the wrist and shoved {V.him} against a parked car in a restaurant lot. A valet called deputies. {V} had bruising on the wrist the next morning. {DL} says {D.he} was pulling {V.him} out of the path of a backing car.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Restaurant Lot Camera", "{D} grabs {V}'s wrist and pushes {V.him} against a car."), E(.forensic, 2, "Photos", "Bruising on {V}'s wrist the next morning.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Pulled Clear", "{DL} says a car was backing out toward {V.him}.")],
        role: "Victim",
        exam: [.direct("What happened in the restaurant lot that night?", "\"We had dinner, and we were arguing as we walked out. {D} grabbed my wrist and shoved me against a parked car.\""), .direct("How did it feel when {D} grabbed you?", "\"It hurt. {D} gripped my wrist hard and pulled, and when I tried to step back {D} pushed me into the car.\""), .direct("What was the injury?", "\"A bruise on my wrist that turned dark by morning, with a sore shoulder where I hit the car door.\""), .direct("Who called the deputies?", "\"A valet who saw it from the lot. I was shaking and had not thought to call anyone.\""), .direct("What had you been arguing about?", "\"Something small from dinner that got bigger as we walked. We were both raising our voices before we reached the lot.\""), .direct("How did you feel afterward?", "\"Shaken and scared. I had never seen {D} act like that before, and I did not know what would happen next.\""), .cross("Was a car moving behind you in the lot?", "\"One was moving behind us, yes. I did not pay attention to it, because I was looking at {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything when grabbing your wrist?", "\"Something about getting out of the way. I was not listening closely, because I was upset.\""), .cross("Did you fall or stumble against the car?", "\"I hit the car with my shoulder. Whether it was a stumble or a shove is something I felt as a shove.\""), .cross("Did you tell the deputies the car was backing up?", "\"I told them we were arguing. I did not think about the car until later, when someone mentioned it.\""), .cross("Did {D} apologize?", "\"Yes, that night, over and over. {D} said it was an accident, and I was too upset to think about it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} grabbed and shoved a girlfriend in a parking lot.", "A grab to get someone out of the way."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry I hurt you.\"",
        truths: ("A text {DL} sent that night read, 'You made me do that.'", "The wide-angle camera shows a car backing toward {V} as {DL} reached."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you shove {V}?", "\"No. I pulled {V.him} clear of a car that was backing toward us. I did not shove anyone.\""), .direct("Why did you grab {V}'s wrist?", "\"It was all I could reach. The car was moving fast, and I had no time to take a better hold.\""), .direct("How did {V} end up against the car?", "\"We both stumbled. I pulled, {V} stepped back, and we both lurched against the parked car beside us.\""), .direct("What about the bruise on {V}'s wrist?", "\"It came from my grip. I held on hard, and I am sorry it left a mark.\""), .direct("Were you and {V} arguing?", "\"Yes, we had been arguing since the table. It was a small thing, and I regret that it was loud.\""), .direct("What did you do after?", "\"I apologized right away. {V} was upset, and I did not know how to calm things down.\""), .cross("The camera shows you shoving {V} against a car, doesn't it?", "\"It shows a fast movement that looks like a shove. I was pulling {V.him} out of the way.\""), .cross("You were arguing right before this, weren't you?", "\"Yes, we were. That is why it looked like something it was not.\""), .cross("You gripped hard enough to leave a bruise, didn't you?", "\"I did. I held tight because I was scared, and I did not realize how hard until I saw it.\""), .cross("You never told the deputies about a backing car, did you?", "\"I did not at first. I was shaken, and I thought they would not believe me.\""), .cross("Did {V} tell you to let go?", "\"Yes, and I did let go. It was seconds, and then {V} walked away.\"")],
        openings: ("After dinner in a restaurant lot, {D} grabbed {V}, {D.his} partner, by the wrist and shoved {V.him} against a parked car. A valet called deputies, and {V} had a dark bruise on the wrist the next morning.", "{D} pulled {V.him} out of the path of a backing car and gripped hard in a panic. A couple in an argument, a moving car, and a bruise do not prove a shove."),
        closings: ("The camera shows {D}'s hand on {V}'s wrist, a push against a car, and a bruise by morning. {V} told the deputies the truth before anyone mentioned a backing car.", "A car moving behind them, a grip made in a rush, and a mark left by fear. {D} meant to protect {V.him}, and the State has not shown a different purpose."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:10 p.m.: the argument starts."), (0, "9:14 p.m.: the grab."), (0, "9:30 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "A parking lot camera and a valet.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a victim in a domestic relationship"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let deletedServerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.deletedServer",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Departing IT Manager Accused of Leaving Script That Wiped Billing Records", "Medical Billing Firm Loses Three Years of Claims"],
        law: "damagingComputers",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Willfully and without authorization destroyed data on the computer network of a medical billing company, causing damage over $1,000.",
        ages: 30...50,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A medical billing company lost three years of claims data on {DATE} when a scheduled script wiped its main database and backups. The script was added under {D}'s login three weeks before {D} resigned. Recovery cost $142,000. {DL} says the login was shared by four people and a vendor patch used the same script name.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Script History", "A scheduled wipe script added under {D}'s login three weeks before {D} resigned."), E(.document, 2, "Resignation Email", "{DL} wrote, 'You'll miss me by the first of March.'"), E(.document, 2, "Recovery Invoice", "$142,000 for data recovery.")],
        defense: [E(.digital, 1, "Shared Login", "The administrator login was used by four people.")],
        role: "Forensic examiner",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a forensic examiner. I analyze logs and scripts to determine what happened inside a system.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A scheduled script wiped the company's main database and its backups, destroying three years of claims data.\""), .direct("What does the script history show?", "\"The wipe script was added under {D}'s login three weeks before {D} resigned.\""), .direct("What did {DL} write when resigning?", "\"'You'll miss me by the first of March.' That email is in evidence.\""), .direct("What did recovery cost?", "\"$142,000 for data recovery. Some data was never recovered.\""), .direct("What was found at {DL}'s new job?", "\"A thumb drive in {D}'s desk that held a copy of the script.\""), .direct("What did the vendor's own logs show about the file name?", "\"The same file name was pushed by the vendor the week the script was added. That means the name alone does not prove who created the wipe script.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} add the script?", "\"I saw the log entry under {D}'s login. I cannot see whose fingers were on the keyboard.\""), .cross("How many people shared that login?", "\"Four people, according to the contractor and company staff.\""), .cross("Did a vendor patch push a file with the same name?", "\"Yes. The vendor's own logs show the same file name pushed that week.\""), .cross("Could the vendor file have been confused with the wipe script?", "\"It is possible. I compared them and found differences, but a hurried admin could confuse them.\""), .cross("Did {DL} still have access after resigning?", "\"I found no logins after the resignation date.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Managed-services contractor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I work for a managed-services contractor. We maintain systems for clients, including this company.\""), .direct("How many people used the administrator login?", "\"Four. Sharing it was a bad practice, but it happened.\""), .direct("Did your company push a patch?", "\"Yes. A vendor patch went out the week the script was added, and it used the same file name.\""), .direct("What does that mean?", "\"It means a script with that name appeared in the system from the vendor, not only from {D}.\""), .direct("What do the logs show?", "\"The vendor's own logs show the same file name pushed that week.\""), .direct("How did {DL} seem at work?", "\"Professional. Unhappy about leaving, but careful with data.\""), .direct("Tell the jury about your company's role at the billing firm.", "\"We are a managed-services contractor. We maintain servers, push vendor patches, and respond to outages for several clients, including the billing company.\""), .direct("What did your company push to the billing firm that week?", "\"A vendor patch with the same file name as the wipe script. It was pushed the same week the script appeared, and our own logs show it.\""), .direct("How many people shared the administrator login?", "\"Four. Sharing it was a poor practice, but it was common at the billing firm, and any of the four could have added a script under that login.\""), .cross("Did the vendor patch wipe backups?", "\"Not that I know. It was meant to update settings.\""), .cross("Who else knew the shared login?", "\"Three other people besides {D}.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} add a script?", "\"No.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever keep scripts on a thumb drive?", "\"I do not know.\""), .cross("Were backups on the same system?", "\"Yes. That was a design weakness.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} left a wipe script set to fire after leaving.", "A shared login and a similarly named vendor patch."),
        allocution: "\"I was angry. I never thought it would reach that far.\"",
        truths: ("A thumb drive in {DL}'s desk at the new job held a copy of the script.", "The vendor's own logs show the same file name pushed the week the script was added."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your role at the company?", "\"I was a database administrator. I maintained jobs and scripts on the main servers.\""), .direct("Did you add the wipe script?", "\"No. The login was used by four people, so my name on a log entry does not mean my hands.\""), .direct("What about the vendor patch?", "\"A vendor pushed a patch the same week with a script that had the same file name. It could have been confused with mine.\""), .direct("What did you mean by 'You'll miss me'?", "\"I meant my skills. I was leaving on bad terms and wanted them to know it.\""), .direct("Why was a copy on your thumb drive?", "\"I kept copies of my own scripts for future use. That is common among administrators.\""), .direct("Did you want to harm the company?", "\"No. I had no reason to destroy years of data.\""), .direct("What was in the thumb drive found in your desk at the new job?", "\"A copy of the script. I kept backups of many scripts I wrote at the old company, and I did not know it was the same one that wiped the data.\""), .cross("The script was added three weeks before you resigned, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the log says. It does not prove I added it.\""), .cross("You wrote that they would miss you, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a parting shot.\""), .cross("A copy was found in your desk, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a copy of a script I used.\""), .cross("You knew the backups were on the same server, didn't you?", "\"I knew how the system worked. That is my job.\""), .cross("$142,000 was spent on recovery, wasn't it?", "\"So I hear. It was not my doing.\"")],
        openings: ("A medical billing company lost three years of claims data when a scheduled script wiped its database and backups. The script was added under {D}'s login three weeks before {D} resigned, with an email warning they would be missed. The State will show the history and the thumb drive.", "The administrator login was shared by four people, and a vendor patch used the same script name. A contractor will tell you how easily the two were confused."),
        closings: ("A wipe script under {D}'s login, a copy at the new job, and a parting email promising they would be missed. {D} destroyed the data.", "A shared login and a vendor patch with the same file name. The State has not proved {D} wrote the wipe script."),
        timeline: [(-21, "The script is added under {DL}'s login."), (-14, "{DL} resigns with a parting email."), (0, "The script runs and the data is wiped."), (2, "The company calls police.")],
        identified: "The script's login history.",
        notDone: ["The vendor's other scripts were never reviewed."],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "searchSeizure"])

    static let tailgateShoveV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.tailgateShove",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Concession Stand Line Argument Ends in a Shove at Youth Ballgame", "Parent Charged After Push Near Trash Cans"],
        law: "simpleAssault",
        spec: "Assaulted {V} by shoving {V.him} with both hands, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At a youth baseball game on {DATE}, {D} and {V} argued over who was next in the concession stand line. {V} says {D} shoved {V.him} into a trash can. {D} says {V} grabbed {D.his} sleeve first. A stand camera caught the shove.",
        state: [E(.video, 2, "Concession Camera", "{D}'s hands on {V}'s shoulders; {V} stumbles into a trash can."), E(.document, 1, "Urgent Care Note", "A scraped palm and a sore shoulder.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Line Witness", "Another parent says {V} grabbed {D}'s sleeve first.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What does the concession camera show?", "\"{D}'s hands on {V}'s shoulders, and {V} stumbling backward into a trash can. The shove itself is clear on the video.\""), .direct("What was the argument about?", "\"Who was next in line at the concession stand during a youth baseball game. Both were frustrated and talking loudly.\""), .direct("What injuries did {V} have?", "\"A scraped palm and a sore shoulder, according to the urgent care note. Nothing broken, and {V} was released the same day.\""), .direct("Where did this happen?", "\"At the concession stand at a youth baseball game, with children, parents, and volunteers all around the line.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"That {V} grabbed {D}'s sleeve first and {D} pushed {V.him} off. {D} said {D.he} did not mean for {V.him} to fall.\""), .direct("What did you do after the shove?", "\"I called the umpire over and checked on {V}. We moved both parents away from the line and told them to cool off.\""), .cross("Does the video show how the encounter started?", "\"No. The angle is cut off, and the start of it is not in the frame.\""), .cross("Did anyone else say {V} grabbed first?", "\"One parent. That parent said {V} reached for {D}'s sleeve before the shove.\""), .cross("Did anyone say {V} did not grab first?", "\"One other person said {V} did not. The accounts are split, and I recorded both.\""), .cross("Did {D} stay at the scene?", "\"Yes. {D} stayed, spoke with me, and helped {V} up from beside the trash can.\""), .cross("Was {V} badly hurt?", "\"No. A scraped palm and a sore shoulder. {V} was treated and sent home that day.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shoved a parent in line.", "A reaction to being grabbed."),
        allocution: "\"I shouldn't have pushed. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} told the volunteers, 'I'll deal with that guy.'", "A second camera angle shows {V} gripping {D}'s sleeve before the push."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was the argument about?", "\"Who was next in line at the concession stand. We both thought it was our turn, and it escalated.\""), .direct("What did {V} do?", "\"Grabbed my sleeve. I felt the pull, and I reacted before I thought about it.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I pushed {V.him} off. I put my hands on {V.his} shoulders and shoved, and {V.he} stumbled backward.\""), .direct("What happened to {V}?", "\"{V} fell into a trash can. I did not mean for that, and I was sorry the moment I saw it.\""), .direct("Was it heated?", "\"We both were. Voices were raised, and neither of us was acting like adults in front of the kids.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I helped {V} up and apologized. I stayed until a deputy came and told the deputy my side.\""), .cross("You pushed {V} with both hands, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, and I know the video shows it plainly. I pushed to get free.\""), .cross("{V} says {V.he} never touched you before the shove, doesn't {V.he}?", "\"That is what {V} says. {V.he} grabbed my sleeve, and one parent saw it.\""), .cross("You were angry about the line, weren't you?", "\"I was irritated. I did not plan to hurt anyone, but I was angry.\""), .cross("Children were watching, weren't they?", "\"Yes. I am ashamed of that. It is not how I want to act at a youth game.\""), .cross("Over a place in line, you shoved someone into a trash can, didn't you?", "\"When you put it like that, it sounds ridiculous. It happened fast, and I wish it had not.\"")],
        openings: ("At a youth baseball game, {D} and {V} argued over a place in the concession line, and a stand camera caught {D} shoving {V} into a trash can. {V} had a scraped palm and a sore shoulder.", "{V} grabbed {D}'s sleeve first, and {D} pushed back for an instant. A heated moment at a ball game is not an assault, and the video does not show the beginning."),
        closings: ("Both hands on {V}'s shoulders, a stumble into a trash can, and a scraped palm. Over a place in line, in front of children, {D} put hands on someone.", "The video starts after {V} grabbed {D}'s sleeve, and a parent saw it. {D} pushed once in a tense moment and helped {V} up."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: the line forms."), (0, "The argument and the shove."), (0, "A volunteer calls deputies.")],
        identified: "A concession stand camera.",
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let nightPharmacyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.nightPharmacy",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Burglar Enters Strip Mall Pharmacy Through Roof Hatch", "Tar Prints Lead Deputies to Roofing Crew"],
        law: "feloniousBE",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Broke and entered a pharmacy, a building in town, with the intent to commit larceny therein.",
        ages: 22...40,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 2:50 a.m. on {DATE}, an alarm sounded at a strip mall pharmacy. Deputies found a cut roof hatch, tar-stained prints leading to the controlled-substance safe, and about 700 tablets missing, and {V}, the pharmacist-owner, said the safe had been locked at close. Tar on the counter matched a sample from {D}'s truck, and {D}'s phone connected to a tower 400 yards away. {DL} says {D.he} was asleep at a partner's home.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Roof Hatch", "A cut hatch and tar-stained boot prints from the roof to the safe.", .search), E(.digital, 3, "Phone Location", "{D}'s phone connects to a tower 400 yards away at 2:50 a.m."), E(.forensic, 2, "Tar Sample", "Roofing tar on the counter matches a sample from {D}'s truck.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Alibi", "{DL} says {D.he} was asleep at a partner's home with the phone charging.")],
        role: "Sheriff's detective",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at the pharmacy that night?", "\"At 2:50 a.m. an alarm sounded at the strip mall pharmacy. Deputies found a cut roof hatch and signs someone had come down from above.\""), .direct("What did you find inside?", "\"Tar-stained boot prints leading from under the hatch to the controlled-substance safe, which was open and emptied.\""), .direct("What was missing?", "\"About 700 tablets. {V}, the pharmacist-owner, told us the safe had been locked at close the night before.\""), .direct("What tied {D} to the scene?", "\"Roofing tar on the counter matched a sample from {D}'s truck, and {D}'s phone connected to a tower 400 yards away at 2:50.\""), .direct("What does {D} do for a living?", "\"{D} is a roofer. {D} works with tar and roofing materials every day, and {D}'s truck had tar on it.\""), .direct("What did {D} say when you asked about that night?", "\"That {D} was asleep at a partner's home. {D} named the partner, and we spoke with that person.\""), .cross("Is roofing tar common?", "\"Among roofers, yes. Tar gets on tools, boots, trucks, and clothes, and other roofers would have it too.\""), .cross("Does a cell tower prove where a phone is?", "\"Only roughly. A tower covers a wide area, and a phone four hundred yards away could be anywhere in that area.\""), .cross("Did you find {D}'s fingerprints in the pharmacy?", "\"No. We found no fingerprints of {D}'s inside, and no footprints that matched {D}'s boots.\""), .cross("Did you find any of the tablets with {D}?", "\"No. We searched {D}'s truck and home and found no missing tablets.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} near the pharmacy?", "\"No. There is no witness who put {D} on the roof or in the parking lot.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's partner",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We are partners. {D} stays at my place a few nights a week, and we have been together a couple of years.\""), .direct("Was {D} at your home on the night of the burglary?", "\"Yes. {D} came over in the evening and we watched television before going to bed.\""), .direct("When did {D} go to sleep?", "\"Asleep by midnight. {D} had an early job the next morning, and went to bed before I did.\""), .direct("Did you wake up that night?", "\"Once, around three. I got up for water, and {D} was asleep beside me when I looked in.\""), .direct("Does {D} work with roofing materials?", "\"Yes, daily. {D} comes home with tar on boots and clothes, and I wash {D}'s work jeans most weeks.\""), .direct("Did you hear {D}'s phone that night?", "\"Not that I recall. {D} keeps the phone charging by the bed, and I do not think it moved.\""), .cross("Were you awake the whole time between midnight and three?", "\"No. I was asleep too. I cannot say what happened between the moment I fell asleep and when I woke.\""), .cross("Could {D} have left and returned while you slept?", "\"I suppose it is possible. I did not hear anything, but I sleep deeply.\""), .cross("What time did you wake the second time?", "\"I did not look at the clock. It was light outside, and {D} was making coffee.\""), .cross("Does {D} have a key to your place?", "\"Yes, and {D} has a few other keys too. That does not change what I told you.\""), .cross("Would you protect {D} if you knew {D} did this?", "\"I would tell you the truth. I told you what I saw, and I am sure about it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered through the roof and emptied the safe.", "A roofer who was asleep miles away."),
        allocution: "\"I was in a bad place with pills. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("Empty bottles with the pharmacy's labels were found in a bin behind a job site where {DL} worked.", "A prybar left on the roof carried the prints of another crew member."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you enter the pharmacy?", "\"No. I never went near that pharmacy, and I did not cut any hatch or open any safe.\""), .direct("Where were you at 2:50 that morning?", "\"Asleep at my partner's. I went to bed before midnight because I had an early job, and I slept soundly.\""), .direct("Why is there tar from your truck on the counter?", "\"Tar gets on everything we own. It was on my truck, my boots, and my tools, and any roofer could have left it.\""), .direct("Why did your phone connect to a tower near the pharmacy?", "\"It covers a wide area. My partner's home is within that tower's range, and the phone was charging by the bed.\""), .direct("Do you know anyone who might have done this?", "\"I do not want to guess. I only know I was asleep, and I did not do it.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Angry and scared. I have never broken into anything, and I work hard for what I earn.\""), .cross("Your truck's tar matched the tar on the counter, didn't it?", "\"So I am told. That tar is on every roofer's truck in this county, and it does not tell you whose.\""), .cross("You are a roofer, and the burglar came through a roof, didn't they?", "\"Yes, and That looks bad, I know. It also makes me one of many people who could have done it.\""), .cross("Your phone connected 400 yards from the pharmacy, didn't it?", "\"Yes, to a tower that also covers my partner's place. The phone was charging in the bedroom.\""), .cross("Nobody saw you asleep at 2:50, did they?", "\"My partner saw me asleep around three. That is as close as anyone can say.\""), .cross("You are the only one connected by both tar and a phone, aren't you?", "\"The tar and the tower both fit where I live and work. That is the problem with the evidence.\"")],
        openings: ("At 2:50 a.m. an alarm sounded at a strip mall pharmacy, and deputies found a cut roof hatch, tar-stained boot prints, and about 700 tablets gone from the controlled-substance safe. Tar and a phone tower tied {D} to the scene.", "{D} is a roofer, and roofing tar is on every roofer's truck, boots, and tools. A cell tower covers a wide area, and {D} was asleep beside a partner at the hour of the burglary."),
        closings: ("A cut roof hatch, tar-stained prints, a matching tar sample from {D}'s truck, and {D}'s phone four hundred yards away at 2:50. The evidence points to the same roofer.", "Tar that is on every roofer, a tower that covers a whole neighborhood, and a partner who saw {D} asleep. The State has coincidence and nothing that puts {D} in the pharmacy."),
        timeline: [(-7, "{DL}'s crew works on a nearby roof."), (0, "2:50 a.m.: the alarm."), (30, "Tar lab results."), (35, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "Tar evidence and phone location.",
        notDone: ["Other crew members were never fingerprinted."],
        mitigating: ["The defendant has a substance use disorder and has sought treatment"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "Patients waited days for their medicine.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"])

    static let churchBooksV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.churchBooks",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Church Financial Secretary Accused of Draining Fund Through Debit Card", "Denomination Audit Finds $108,900 Missing"],
        law: "embezzlement100k",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "As financial secretary, embezzled $108,900 from a church congregation.",
        ages: 44...63,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A regional denomination audit found $108,900 missing from a church's accounts. For three years {D}, the volunteer financial secretary, used a debit card on a second account for groceries, fuel, and transfers to {D.his} own bank. {DL} says the board chair told {D.him} to use church funds to keep the roof loan current until the annual meeting.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Export", "Debit purchases and transfers totaling $108,900 on a card held by {D}."), E(.video, 2, "ATM Camera", "{D} withdraws cash on forty-one dates."), E(.document, 2, "Audit Letter", "The denomination's audit shows no board vote.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Board Chair Email", "'Use the building fund to keep the roof loan current.'")],
        role: "Denominational auditor",
        exam: [.direct("What did your audit find?", "\"$108,900 missing from the church's accounts over three years. The money went through a second account with a debit card.\""), .direct("Who held the card?", "\"{D}, the volunteer financial secretary. The card was ordered under the church's tax number.\""), .direct("What was it used for?", "\"Groceries, fuel, and transfers to {D}'s own bank account. The bank export lists them line by line.\""), .direct("What does the ATM camera show?", "\"{D} withdrawing cash on forty-one different dates.\""), .direct("Was there a board vote?", "\"No. The denomination's audit found no board vote approving the card or the spending.\""), .direct("What did {DL} tell you?", "\"That the board chair told {D} to use church funds to keep the roof loan current until the annual meeting.\""), .direct("What did the board chair's email say, and did it authorize groceries and fuel?", "\"The email said to use the building fund to keep the roof loan current. It did not mention groceries, fuel, or transfers to a personal account, and no board vote approved them.\""), .cross("Did the board chair send an email to {DL}?", "\"Yes. It says to use the building fund to keep the roof loan current.\""), .cross("Does that email mention groceries or fuel?", "\"No. It mentions only the building fund and the roof loan.\""), .cross("Did the roof loan payments get made?", "\"Some were. I traced them, and they do not account for the full $108,900.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the debit card?", "\"The card was in a separate account that the board did not review.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate with the audit?", "\"Yes. {D} handed over records and answered my questions.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Board chair",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I chair the church board. I oversee finances along with the pastor.\""), .direct("Did you send an email to {DL}?", "\"Yes. It said to use the building fund to keep the roof loan current.\""), .direct("What else did it say?", "\"That we would sort it at the annual meeting. I meant the loan only.\""), .direct("Did you approve a second debit card?", "\"No. I did not know of one.\""), .direct("Did you approve groceries or fuel?", "\"Never. That was not what I meant.\""), .direct("How do you feel about {DL}?", "\"Betrayed, but also sad. {D} was trusted for years.\""), .direct("Tell us how you oversee the church's money as board chair.", "\"I chair the board, and the financial secretary handles the day-to-day books. We review reports at meetings, and we rely on the volunteer to keep us informed.\""), .direct("What did you tell {D} about paying the roof loan?", "\"I told {D} in an email to use the building fund to keep the roof loan current, and said we would sort it out at the annual meeting.\""), .direct("Did you ever approve spending on groceries, fuel, or personal transfers?", "\"No. I never approved any of that. My email was only about the roof loan, and I did not know about the second debit card until the audit.\""), .direct("Did anyone on the board know that a second debit card existed?", "\"No. Nobody on the board knew about the second card, and the audit was the first time I heard about it. I would never have approved a card like that.\""), .cross("Did the board vote on the roof loan plan?", "\"Not formally.\""), .cross("Did you check the accounts?", "\"Not often enough.\""), .cross("Did you ask for receipts?", "\"Sometimes. Not always.\""), .cross("Did {DL} tell you about the card?", "\"No.\""), .cross("Did you know about forty-one withdrawals?", "\"No.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} treated a church's funds as a personal account.", "A volunteer following a chair's instruction."),
        allocution: "\"I took what was not mine and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A second debit card was ordered under the church's tax number, a card only {DL} knew about.", "The board chair's email said to use the building fund and 'we'll sort it at the annual meeting.'"),
        defendant: [.direct("What is your role at the church?", "\"I volunteer as the financial secretary. I keep records and handle deposits.\""), .direct("Why did you use church funds?", "\"The board chair told me to keep the roof loan current using the building fund until the annual meeting.\""), .direct("Why a second debit card?", "\"It made paying the loan simpler. I ordered it and used it for church needs.\""), .direct("What about the groceries and fuel?", "\"I made some personal purchases and meant to repay them. I let it slide, and that was wrong.\""), .direct("What about the transfers to your bank?", "\"I moved money back and forth for convenience. I should have kept the accounts separate.\""), .direct("Do you accept responsibility?", "\"I accept that I mixed things I should not have. I am sorry for the trouble.\""), .direct("What did you spend the debit card on, and who knew about it?", "\"I used it for the roof loan and also for groceries, fuel, and transfers to my own bank. The second card was ordered under the church's tax number, and only I knew about it.\""), .cross("$108,900 went through that card, didn't it?", "\"The bank says so. I did not add it up.\""), .cross("You withdrew cash forty-one times, didn't you?", "\"If the camera shows it, yes.\""), .cross("No board vote approved the card, did it?", "\"Not formally. I relied on the chair's word.\""), .cross("Only you knew about the second card, didn't you?", "\"Mostly. I did not talk about it.\""), .cross("You used church money for groceries, didn't you?", "\"Some, yes. I should not have.\"")],
        openings: ("A denomination audit found $108,900 missing from a church's accounts over three years. {D}, the volunteer financial secretary, used a second debit card for groceries, fuel, and transfers to {D}'s own bank. The State will show the bank export and the ATM camera.", "A board chair's email said to use the building fund to keep the roof loan current. {D} says the chair told {D} to do it, and the chair will tell you what was meant."),
        closings: ("A second card only {D} knew about, forty-one withdrawals, no board vote, and $108,900 gone. {D} used the church's money as a personal account.", "An email from the board chair about the roof loan. The State has not proved {D} had permission for groceries and personal transfers, but it has not proved intent to steal either."),
        timeline: [(-1000, "The second account is opened."), (-300, "The roof loan payments start."), (0, "The audit begins."), (60, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "{DL} held the card on the account.",
        notDone: ["The board chair was never interviewed by investigators."],
        aggravating: ["The reports to the congregation were falsified for three years"],
        mitigating: ["Part of the money paid the congregation's roof loan", "No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let fireAlarmPullV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fireAlarmPull",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Hotel Guest Pulls Fire Alarm at 3 A.M. After Noise Dispute", "118 Guests Evacuated, No Fire Found"],
        law: "falseReport",
        spec: "Willfully made a false report that a building was on fire by pulling a fire alarm, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...50,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Two engines were sent to a hotel at 3:12 a.m. on {DATE} when a fire alarm sounded. There was no fire. A hallway camera showed {D} step out of a room and pull the lever after complaining about a party next door. {DL} says {D.he} thought the lever opened a locked stairwell door.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hallway Camera", "{D} leaves Room 214 and pulls the station at 3:12 a.m."), E(.document, 2, "Fire Department Log", "Two engines; 118 guests evacuated.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Mistook It", "{DL} says {D.he} thought the lever released a stairwell door.")],
        role: "Hotel night manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am the hotel night manager. I oversee the desk, handle complaints, and respond to alarms.\""), .direct("What happened at 3:12 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"The fire alarm sounded. Two engines were sent and 118 guests were evacuated into the cold.\""), .direct("Was there a fire?", "\"No. We checked every floor and found no fire, no smoke, and no heat.\""), .direct("What does the hallway camera show?", "\"{D} stepping out of Room 214 and pulling the station at 3:12 a.m.\""), .direct("What had {DL} complained about?", "\"A party next door. {D} had called the desk about noise earlier.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say to the clerk?", "\"'I'll clear them out myself.' That's how it looked to me at the time, as best I can recall.\""), .direct("What happened to the hotel guests when the alarm sounded?", "\"All 118 guests were evacuated into the cold at about three in the morning. Two engines arrived, firefighters checked every floor, and it took until 3:40 to clear the building.\""), .direct("What did {D} say to the desk clerk before the alarm?", "\"{D} complained twice about a party next door and then said, I'll clear them out myself. A few minutes later, the hallway camera shows {D} pulling the lever.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} pull the lever?", "\"I watched the hallway camera. I was at the desk when the alarm sounded.\""), .cross("Is the pull station clearly marked?", "\"It is red but older. It sits beside an unmarked exit door, which can confuse guests.\""), .cross("Had anyone pulled it by mistake before?", "\"Yes. Another guest pulled it by mistake the month before.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to leave the hotel during the alarm?", "\"No. {D} walked out with the other guests.\""), .cross("Did {DL} admit pulling it?", "\"Yes. {D} said so right away and said it was a mistake.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pulled a fire alarm to end a noisy party.", "A guest who mistook a lever for a door release."),
        allocution: "\"I was exhausted and angry. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} told the desk clerk, 'I'll clear them out myself.'", "The pull station sat beside an unmarked exit door, and another guest pulled it by mistake the month before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you awake at 3 a.m.?", "\"A party next door kept me up for hours. I had already called the desk twice.\""), .direct("What did you do at 3:12?", "\"I stepped into the hall and pulled a lever I thought opened a locked stairwell door.\""), .direct("Why did you think that?", "\"It sat beside an unmarked exit door. It looked like a release for the stairwell.\""), .direct("Did you know it was a fire alarm?", "\"No. I thought it was a door release. When the alarm blared I realized what I had done.\""), .direct("What did you say to the clerk?", "\"I said I would clear them out myself. I meant I would go talk to them.\""), .direct("Do you regret it?", "\"Yes. Everyone was pulled out of bed because of my mistake.\""), .direct("Why did you pull the lever in the hallway at 3:12?", "\"I thought it released a stairwell door. It sat next to an unmarked exit door, and I did not think it was a fire alarm, so I pulled it without reading it.\""), .direct("What did you say to the desk clerk before you pulled it?", "\"I told the clerk I would clear the party out myself. I meant I would knock on the door, and I did not mean I would set off the alarm.\""), .cross("You were angry at the party, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was tired and frustrated.\""), .cross("You told the clerk you would clear them out, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it, but I meant a talk.\""), .cross("The station is red and labeled, isn't it?", "\"It looked faded to me and sat beside an unmarked door.\""), .cross("118 guests were evacuated, weren't they?", "\"So I am told. I feel awful about it.\""), .cross("You pulled the lever, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did.\"")],
        openings: ("Two engines were sent to a hotel at 3:12 a.m. when a fire alarm sounded. There was no fire, and a hallway camera shows {D} step out of Room 214 and pull the station after complaining about a party next door. The State will show the video and the log.", "A pull station sat next to an unmarked exit door, and another guest had pulled it by mistake the month before. {D} says {D.he} mistook it for a door release."),
        closings: ("A guest angry about a party, a promise to clear them out, and a pulled alarm with no fire. 118 guests were evacuated.", "A pull station beside an unmarked exit and a past mistaken pull. The State has not proved {D} knew it was a fire alarm."),
        timeline: [(0, "2:30 a.m.: {DL} complains twice."), (0, "3:12 a.m.: the alarm sounds."), (0, "3:40 a.m.: engines clear the building.")],
        identified: "The hallway camera.",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let snowbankV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.snowbank",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Deputy Found Dead in Culvert After Late Pickup in Sleet", "SUV Data Shows Hard Stop and Reverse"],
        law: "murder2",
        threshold: 3,
        spec: "Killed {V} by striking {V.him} with a motor vehicle while impaired, with malice.",
        ages: 33...46,
        victim: true,
        summary: "During a sleet storm on {DATE}, {D} picked up {V}, a county sheriff's deputy and {D.his} partner, after a night shift. {V} was found dead the next morning in a culvert on a rural road, killed by a head injury and the cold. {D}'s SUV had a cracked bumper cover, and its log showed a hard stop and a reverse at 2:41 a.m. {DL} says {V} got out after an argument and walked.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Vehicle Data", "The SUV's log shows a hard stop and a reverse at 2:41 a.m."), E(.forensic, 2, "Medical Examiner", "A head injury consistent with a vehicle strike, then hypothermia."), E(.physical, 2, "Bumper Cover", "A cracked cover with fibers matching {V}'s uniform jacket.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Dispatch Log", "A tow driver reported a figure on the shoulder near the culvert at 2:55 a.m.")],
        role: "Sheriff's investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What does the SUV's vehicle log show?", "\"A hard stop and a reverse at 2:41 a.m. on that night, on the rural road where {V} was found.\""), .direct("How did {V} die?", "\"A head injury and exposure. The medical examiner found a head injury consistent with a vehicle strike, followed by hypothermia.\""), .direct("Where was {V} found?", "\"In a culvert beside a rural road the next morning. It had been a sleet storm, and {V} was partly covered by ice.\""), .direct("What was found on the SUV?", "\"A cracked bumper cover with fibers that match {V}'s uniform jacket. We seized it under a search warrant.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you?", "\"That {D} picked up {V} after a night shift, that they argued, and that {V} got out of the SUV and walked off.\""), .direct("When was {D} tested for alcohol?", "\"Hours later. By the time we tested, a fair amount of time had passed, and {D} admitted drinking earlier.\""), .cross("Could a fall into a culvert cause the head injury?", "\"A fall into a culvert is possible. A fall onto ice or a concrete edge can cause that kind of injury.\""), .cross("Did the examiner rule it a homicide?", "\"The examiner described the injury as consistent with a vehicle strike. Consistent is not the same as proven.\""), .cross("Could the bumper cover have been cracked earlier?", "\"It could. {D} says a snowbank cracked it earlier, and I cannot rule that out.\""), .cross("Why would the SUV reverse at 2:41?", "\"Several reasons are possible, including turning back to look for someone. The log does not say why.\""), .cross("Did {D} call anyone for help that night?", "\"No. {D} went home. I cannot say whether {D} knew what had happened.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Accident reconstructionist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do for a living?", "\"I reconstruct accidents. I analyze vehicle damage, injuries, and scene evidence to work out how crashes and falls happen.\""), .direct("Did you review the injuries in this case?", "\"Yes. I reviewed the examiner's report and the photographs of the injuries, along with the culvert and the roadway.\""), .direct("Do the injuries fit a car strike?", "\"Not clearly. They also fit a fall, especially onto an icy edge. The injury alone does not tell you which.\""), .direct("What did you see on the bumper cover?", "\"A crack, and some fibers. Fibers can transfer in many ways, and a bumper that touched a jacket does not prove a strike.\""), .direct("What was the weather that night?", "\"Sleet. The road was glazed with ice, and the culvert edge would have been slick and dangerous for anyone walking.\""), .direct("Could {V} have fallen while walking along that road?", "\"Yes. People fall on ice, and a person in a heavy uniform jacket could slip and hit the culvert.\""), .cross("Could the SUV have struck {V}?", "\"It is possible. I cannot rule it out, and the log and fibers both fit that possibility.\""), .cross("Does the hard stop and reverse fit a strike?", "\"It could. It could also fit a driver who stopped suddenly to look for someone.\""), .cross("Did you see any tire marks or skid marks?", "\"Not with certainty. The sleet and the snow covered most of the marks by the time anyone looked.\""), .cross("Are you being paid for your opinion?", "\"Yes, for my time, as in every case. My opinion does not change with the fee.\""), .cross("Can you say what happened to {V}?", "\"No. I can only say what the evidence does and does not show, and it does not settle the question.\"")],
        theory: ("{D}, drunk and angry, struck a partner with an SUV and left {V.him} in the cold.", "A partner who walked off alone and fell."),
        allocution: "\"I loved {V}. I did not hit {V.him}. I live with not knowing.\"",
        truths: ("A farm camera, found later, shows the SUV reversing over the roadside at 2:41 a.m.", "The tow driver later identified {V} walking alone at 2:55 a.m., after the SUV was gone."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened that night?", "\"We argued, and {V} got out of the SUV. {V} said to stop, and I did, and {V} started walking along the road.\""), .direct("What were you arguing about?", "\"Something from work. It got heated, and {V} was upset and wanted out of the SUV.\""), .direct("Why did the SUV reverse?", "\"I turned back to look for {V.him}. I felt bad about leaving {V.him} in the sleet and wanted to offer a ride.\""), .direct("Did you find {V}?", "\"No. I did not see {V} again. The sleet was heavy, and I could not find where {V.he} went.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking?", "\"Two beers earlier that night. I did not think I was impaired, but I should not have been driving.\""), .direct("What about the cracked bumper?", "\"A snowbank earlier. I hit it while backing out of a parking space before the shift ended.\""), .cross("You were drinking and driving in a sleet storm, weren't you?", "\"Two beers, hours earlier. I know I should not have been behind the wheel.\""), .cross("Your log shows a hard stop and a reverse at 2:41, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. That was when I turned back to look for {V}. I did not hit anyone.\""), .cross("Fibers from {V}'s jacket were on your bumper, weren't they?", "\"So I am told. I do not know how they got there, and I did not hit {V.him}.\""), .cross("You never called for help, did you?", "\"No. I went home. I did not know anything had happened, and I thought {V} would be fine.\""), .cross("You left a colleague on a sleet-covered road, didn't you?", "\"I did not leave {V.him}. {V.he} got out and walked, and I looked for {V.him} before I gave up.\"")],
        openings: ("During a sleet storm, {D} drove {V}, a deputy, home after a night shift. {V} was found dead the next morning in a culvert, and {D}'s SUV had a cracked bumper cover with fibers from {V}'s jacket and a hard stop and reverse at 2:41 a.m.", "{V} got out of the SUV after an argument and walked off into the sleet. {D} turned back to look for {V.him}, never found {V.him}, and went home without knowing what had happened."),
        closings: ("A hard stop, a reverse, a cracked bumper with fibers from {V}'s jacket, and a head injury that fits a strike. {D} had been drinking and did not call for help.", "A culvert on an icy road, an injury that fits a fall as well as a car, and a driver who turned back to look. The State must prove {D} struck {V}, and the evidence leaves that open."),
        timeline: [(0, "1 a.m.: {D} picks up {V}."), (0, "2:41 a.m.: the SUV stops and reverses."), (0, "2:55 a.m.: a tow driver sees a figure."), (1, "7 a.m.: {V} is found in the culvert."), (30, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "{D} was the last person with {V}, and the SUV was damaged.",
        notDone: ["No one canvassed the farms along the road that night."],
        aggravating: ["{DL} left {V} in freezing conditions"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "My child lay out in the cold. Somebody knows more.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "lesserIncluded"])

    static let pillDiversionV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pillDiversion",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Nursing Aide Accused of Pocketing Oxycodone From Assisted Living Med Cart", "Count Sheet Gap Leads to Aide's Bag"],
        law: "possSchedII",
        spec: "Possessed a Schedule II controlled substance, oxycodone, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A nurse at an assisted living facility found eleven oxycodone tablets short on {DATE}. A med room camera showed {D}, an aide, sliding a blister card into a scrub pocket. A search of {D}'s bag turned up eleven tablets in a pill organizer. {DL} says {D.he} was moving the card to a locked drawer.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Med Room Camera", "{D} slips a blister card into a scrub pocket."), E(.physical, 3, "Pill Organizer", "Eleven tablets in {D}'s bag.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Count Sheet", "The count sheet had been corrected twice by hand.")],
        role: "Director of nursing",
        exam: [.direct("What was missing from the medication count?", "\"Eleven oxycodone tablets. I found the shortage when I reconciled the blister card against the count sheet that day.\""), .direct("What did the med room camera show?", "\"{D}, an aide, sliding a blister card into a scrub pocket. The card is not returned to the cart on the video.\""), .direct("What did a search of {D}'s bag turn up?", "\"A pill organizer holding eleven tablets. The number matches the number missing from the card.\""), .direct("Are aides allowed to handle controlled medications?", "\"No. Aides do not handle controlled drugs. Only nurses sign for and administer them, and aides are not in the count.\""), .direct("Was the count sheet corrected?", "\"Twice. The first correction was made before the shortage was reported, and a second was made afterward.\""), .direct("Who corrected the count sheet?", "\"A shift nurse. I have the sheet showing the initials, and I spoke with the nurse about it.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take any tablet from the card?", "\"No. The camera shows the card going into a pocket. I did not see tablets leave the card.\""), .cross("Was the med room locked?", "\"It was supposed to be. Staff in the room that day had keys, and the door was opened several times.\""), .cross("Can an aide ever hold a card for a nurse?", "\"Rarely. If a nurse asks, an aide may move a card, but that should be recorded.\""), .cross("Could the count sheet have been wrong from the start?", "\"It could. Two corrections show there was confusion, and I am not sure the first count was accurate.\""), .cross("Did {D} deny having the organizer?", "\"No. {D} said it was {D.his} own organizer and offered the bag for inspection.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pocketed oxycodone from a med cart.", "An aide putting a card away."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I was hurting.\"",
        truths: ("The tablets in the organizer carried the facility's lot code.", "A nurse later admitted she had miscounted and corrected the sheet without telling anyone."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take pills?", "\"No. I did not take any pills from that card. I was moving it, not emptying it.\""), .direct("Why did you put the card in your pocket?", "\"To reach the drawer key. I had a hand full of supplies, and I tucked the card away for a second.\""), .direct("Where were you going with the card?", "\"To the locked drawer. A nurse had told me to put it there until the count was done.\""), .direct("What is in the pill organizer?", "\"It is mine, for my own daily vitamins and medicine. I carry it in my bag, and I keep it at work.\""), .direct("Why are there eleven tablets in it?", "\"I cannot fully explain it. I did not put oxycodone in my organizer, and I do not know how it came to hold those tablets.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"Humiliated. I have worked in care for years, and I would never take from the people I look after.\""), .cross("You put the card in your scrub pocket, didn't you?", "\"Yes, briefly. I had my hands full, and I thought it was quicker than setting it down.\""), .cross("An aide does not handle controlled drugs, does an aide?", "\"Not normally. A nurse asked me to move the card, and I did what I was told.\""), .cross("Eleven tablets are in your organizer, and eleven were missing, aren't they?", "\"So I am told. I cannot explain it, and I did not take them.\""), .cross("You did not tell anyone about moving the card, did you?", "\"I told the nurse who asked me. I did not write it down, and I wish I had.\""), .cross("Why is oxycodone in a vitamin organizer?", "\"It should not be. I do not know how it got there, and I want to know too.\"")],
        openings: ("An assisted living nurse found eleven oxycodone tablets short. A camera showed {D}, an aide, slide a blister card into a scrub pocket, and a search of {D}'s bag turned up eleven tablets in a pill organizer.", "{D} was moving a card to a locked drawer at a nurse's request, with a handful of supplies. Count sheets were corrected twice, and an honest question remains about how the count went wrong."),
        closings: ("A card in a pocket, eleven tablets gone, and eleven tablets in {D}'s own organizer. An aide has no business with controlled drugs, and the numbers match.", "A nurse's errand, a count sheet corrected twice, and a camera that cannot show a single tablet leaving a card. The State must prove {D} took them."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{DL} starts at the facility."), (0, "6 a.m.: {DL} pockets a card."), (0, "7 a.m.: the shortage is noticed."), (1, "The bag is searched.")],
        identified: "A med room camera.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let longDriveV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.longDrive",
        category: .robbery,
        headlines: ["Ex-Partner Charged With Kidnapping After Ride Past Every Exit", "Smartwatch Text Brought Troopers to Pickup Truck"],
        law: "kidnapping2",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Unlawfully restrained and removed {V} for the purpose of terrorizing {V.him}.",
        ages: 26...42,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} rode with {D}, a former partner, to pick up belongings. {D} drove past the exit and stayed on the interstate for three hours. {V} sent a text from a smartwatch, and troopers stopped the truck at a weigh station. {DL} says {V} agreed to go and could have asked to stop at any time.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Location Share", "Live location shows the truck passing three exits at 70 mph."), E(.digital, 2, "Watch Text", "'Not letting me out, call 911.'")],
        defense: [E(.digital, 1, "Morning Messages", "Friendly texts between {D} and {V} that morning.")],
        role: "Responding trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you stopped the truck?", "\"{V} shaking in the passenger seat of {D}'s truck at a weigh station, frightened and on the verge of tears.\""), .direct("What did {V} tell you?", "\"That {D} would not take any exit during a three hour drive. {V} said {V.he} had asked to stop and been refused.\""), .direct("What does the location share show?", "\"The truck passing three exits at 70 miles an hour, live on the map, over about three hours.\""), .direct("What was the watch text?", "\"'Not letting me out, call 911.' It was sent from {V}'s smartwatch while the truck was on the interstate.\""), .direct("Was {V} bound or restrained?", "\"No. {V} was not tied, taped, or held down by hand.\""), .direct("Was the door locked?", "\"The child locks were on. A passenger could not open the rear doors from inside, and I confirmed that at the scene.\""), .cross("Had {V} agreed to ride with {D}?", "\"Yes. {V} agreed to go to pick up belongings, and got into the truck willingly.\""), .cross("Did {V} try to open a door during the drive?", "\"I do not know. {V} did not tell me that, and I have no evidence of an attempt.\""), .cross("Did {D} resist when you stopped the truck?", "\"No. {D} pulled over, turned off the engine, and answered my questions.\""), .cross("Did {D} say why the drive was so long?", "\"{D} said they needed to talk, and the conversation took longer than planned.\""), .cross("Was {V} injured?", "\"No. {V} was frightened but not hurt. We offered medical attention, and {V} declined.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Gas station clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do at the station?", "\"I work the counter at a gas station near the interstate. I ring up drinks, fuel, and snacks all day.\""), .direct("Did you see {V} at your station?", "\"Yes. {V} walked in alone, looked around, and walked out again a few minutes later.\""), .direct("How did {V} seem?", "\"Quiet and a little tense. {V} did not say anything to me, and I thought nothing was wrong.\""), .direct("Was the door to the station open?", "\"Yes. It was a warm day, and the door was propped open. {V} walked right past it.\""), .direct("Did you see {D}?", "\"I saw a person in a truck at the pump. I did not talk with that person, and the person stayed in the truck.\""), .direct("How long was {V} at the station?", "\"A few minutes. {V} walked around the store and left. I did not see anyone stop {V}.\""), .cross("Did {V} ask you for help?", "\"No. {V} did not say a word to me, and I did not notice anything that made me worry.\""), .cross("Would you have helped if {V} had asked?", "\"Of course. I would have called the police right away if anyone had said anything.\""), .cross("Did you notice if {V} looked frightened?", "\"Not clearly. In hindsight, {V} may have looked tense, but I did not think much of it.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} get back in the truck?", "\"Yes. {V} walked back and got in on the passenger side. I did not see anyone force it.\""), .cross("Did you see whether {V} had a phone?", "\"I did not notice. {V} was not on a phone that I saw.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove {V} for hours without a way out to frighten {V.him}.", "A tense ride that {V} agreed to take."),
        allocution: "\"I frightened you, and I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{V}'s phone was in {DL}'s glove box and the rear child locks were engaged.", "The station camera shows {V} walking past an open door and a clerk without asking for help."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you drive so far?", "\"We needed to talk. We had a lot to settle, and the conversation kept going, and the miles went by.\""), .direct("Did you stop at all?", "\"At a gas station, where {V} went inside. I stayed in the truck, and {V} came back on {V.his} own.\""), .direct("Could {V} get out?", "\"Yes. {V} could have asked me to stop at any time, and I would have pulled over.\""), .direct("What about the child locks?", "\"A habit. I had them on from carrying a child in the truck earlier, and I forgot to turn them off.\""), .direct("Did {V} ask you to stop?", "\"Not that I heard. If {V} had, I would have stopped. We were talking, and I lost track of the exits.\""), .direct("What did you do when the trooper stopped you?", "\"I pulled over and cooperated. I was surprised and sorry that {V} felt frightened.\""), .cross("You drove past three exits and kept going for three hours, didn't you?", "\"We were talking, and I did not turn off. I see how it looks.\""), .cross("The child locks were on, weren't they?", "\"Yes, on the rear doors. It was a habit, and I did not think about it.\""), .cross("{V} sent a text that said 'Not letting me out, call 911,' didn't {V.he}?", "\"That is what the text says. I did not know {V} sent it until the trooper told me.\""), .cross("You never offered to take {V} back, did you?", "\"I should have. I kept thinking we were close to finishing the talk.\""), .cross("You were the driver, and you controlled where the truck went, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I did, and I take responsibility for how long the drive went.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} rode with {D}, a former partner, to pick up belongings, and {D} drove past the exit and stayed on the interstate for three hours. A smartwatch text read, 'Not letting me out, call 911,' and troopers stopped the truck at a weigh station.", "{V} agreed to go, walked into a gas station alone, and never asked anyone for help. A long, awkward talk in a truck is not a kidnapping."),
        closings: ("Three exits passed at 70, a text asking for 911, and child locks on the rear doors. {D} controlled the truck and never let {V} out.", "{V} could have spoken to a clerk, left the truck, or asked {D} to stop. The State must prove {D} kept {V} against {V.his} will, and the evidence does not show it."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 a.m.: {V} gets into the truck."), (0, "10:30 a.m.: the truck passes the first missed exit."), (0, "12:15 p.m.: the smartwatch text."), (20, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "{V} identified {D}, and the truck was stopped by troopers.",
        notDone: ["The gas station clerk was never interviewed."],
        aggravating: ["{DL} threatened {V}"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let mercyKillingV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.mercyKilling",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Husband, 84, Walks Into Sheriff's Office to Report Wife's Death", "'She Asked Me': Elderly Spouse Charged With First-Degree Murder"],
        law: "murder1",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "With premeditation and deliberation, killed {V}, the defendant's wife of 61 years, by giving her a fatal dose of her own medication.",
        ages: 84...84,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {D}, 84, walked into the sheriff's office with a handwritten letter and told the desk deputy that {V}, {D.his} wife of sixty-one years, was dead at home. {V} had advanced Parkinson's disease with dementia and had been in constant pain. Deputies found {V} in bed. A hospice morphine bottle was empty. {DL} says {V} asked for this years ago and again in a clear moment.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Letter", "A handwritten letter on the kitchen table explaining and apologizing."), E(.forensic, 3, "Toxicology", "A lethal level of morphine."), E(.document, 2, "Hospice Log", "One bottle of morphine unaccounted for.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Advance Directive", "{V}'s signed wish to decline life-prolonging care.")],
        role: "Sheriff's detective",
        exam: [.direct("How did this case begin?", "\"{D}, 84, walked into the sheriff's office with a handwritten letter and told the desk deputy that {V}, {D.his} spouse of sixty-one years, was dead at home.\""), .direct("What did you find at the house?", "\"{V} lying in bed, peaceful, and an empty morphine bottle on the nightstand. There were no signs of a struggle.\""), .direct("What did the letter say?", "\"It explained that {V} had asked for relief and apologized. It was handwritten and left on the kitchen table.\""), .direct("What did toxicology show?", "\"A lethal level of morphine in {V}'s blood. The examiner ruled the cause of death as morphine toxicity.\""), .direct("What did the hospice log show?", "\"One bottle of morphine unaccounted for. It was the same bottle found empty beside the bed.\""), .direct("How did {D} behave when you met?", "\"Calm and clear. {D} did not run, did not deny anything, and said {D.he} was ready to accept what came.\""), .cross("Was {V} suffering?", "\"The hospice notes say so. {V} had advanced Parkinson's disease with dementia and was in constant pain.\""), .cross("Did {D} flee?", "\"No. {D} came to us on {D.his} own, carrying the letter, and gave a full account.\""), .cross("Did {D} have any criminal history?", "\"None. {D} has lived here a long time with no record of any kind.\""), .cross("Did {D} take anything for {D.himself}?", "\"No. We found nothing to suggest personal gain. {D} cared for {V} at home for years.\""), .cross("Was {D} cooperative throughout?", "\"Completely. {D} answered every question and showed us where everything was in the house.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Grandchild",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How are you related to {D} and {V}?", "\"I am their grandchild. I visited often during {V}'s illness and helped with errands and meals.\""), .direct("How was {V}'s health?", "\"Awful. {V} was in pain every day and confused most of the time, and rarely knew where {V.he} was.\""), .direct("What was {D}'s role in {V}'s care?", "\"{D} did almost everything. {D} fed, bathed, and turned {V}, and slept in a chair beside the bed most nights.\""), .direct("How did {D} seem in recent months?", "\"Exhausted and heartbroken. {D} had lost weight and talked about how much {V} was suffering.\""), .direct("Did {V} ever talk about wanting to die?", "\"Years ago, when {V} was clear, {V.he} said {V.he} never wanted to live like that. I heard it myself once.\""), .direct("Did you have hospice help?", "\"Yes, a hospice team visited a few times a week. They kept {V} on morphine for pain and checked in with {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you what {D.he} planned?", "\"No. {D} never told me. I learned afterward, when the sheriff called.\""), .cross("Were you surprised?", "\"Yes. I was shocked, though I understood how worn down {D} was.\""), .cross("Did you ever worry {D} might hurt {V}?", "\"No. {D} loved {V} deeply. I never imagined this.\""), .cross("Did you consult a doctor about options?", "\"The hospice team discussed comfort care. No one discussed ending {V}'s life.\""), .cross("Do you think {D} did the right thing?", "\"I do not know. I know {D} acted from love and from exhaustion, and I know the law sees it differently.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} planned and carried out a fatal dose for a spouse.", "A husband honoring a wish after sixty-one years."),
        allocution: "\"I kept my word. I will answer for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} wrote in a calendar the week before, 'Saturday. Enough.'", "A recording on {V}'s tablet shows {V.him} asking {D} in a clear moment to 'let me go.'"),
        defendant: [.direct("What did you do?", "\"I gave {V.him} the morphine. I helped {V.him} take the bottle, and I stayed with {V.him} until the end.\""), .direct("Why?", "\"{V.He} asked me. Many times, over years, and again in a clear moment. I could not stand to watch the pain.\""), .direct("Did you plan it?", "\"For a week. I thought about it and wrote the letter, and I did not do it in a rush.\""), .direct("Did you tell anyone?", "\"No. I did not tell the hospice, my family, or anyone. I knew they would try to stop me.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I wrote the letter, sat with {V.him} for a while, and walked to the sheriff's office to tell them.\""), .direct("What do you want the court to know?", "\"I loved {V.him} for sixty-one years. I did what {V.he} asked, and I am ready for whatever comes.\""), .cross("You knew giving morphine in that amount would kill {V}, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I knew. That was what {V.he} asked for, and I understood what it would do.\""), .cross("You planned it for a week, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not act on impulse. I thought about it carefully.\""), .cross("You told no one, even hospice, did you?", "\"No one. I was afraid they would stop me or take {V.him} away.\""), .cross("{V} had dementia, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes, and that is why I say {V.he} asked me in a clear moment. {V.He} was not always clear, but {V.he} was that day.\""), .cross("You are not a doctor, are you?", "\"No. I am only a spouse who watched someone I loved suffer.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, 84, walked into the sheriff's office with a handwritten letter and said that {V}, {D.his} spouse of sixty-one years, was dead at home. Toxicology found a lethal level of morphine, and a hospice bottle was empty.", "{V} had advanced Parkinson's disease with dementia and constant pain, and had asked for relief for years. {D} acted from love, planned nothing for gain, and turned {D.himself} in."),
        closings: ("A lethal dose of morphine, a week of planning, and no one told. Whatever the love behind it, {D} ended {V}'s life, and the law treats that as a killing.", "Sixty-one years, a spouse in constant pain, and a request made in a clear moment. {D} did not run, did not hide, and did not gain from it."),
        timeline: [(-2000, "{V} is diagnosed."), (-14, "{V} asks again to be let go."), (0, "Saturday night: {DL} gives {V} the dose."), (0, "Sunday morning: {DL} walks into the sheriff's office."), (1, "Charged with first-degree murder.")],
        identified: "{D} reported it in person.",
        notDone: ["Hospice staff were never asked about {V}'s stated wishes."],
        aggravating: ["The victim was especially vulnerable due to age or disability"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record", "The defendant has a support system in the community"],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        impact: "She hummed hymns some days. Please do not forget she was still here.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let coachCyberstalkingV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.coachCyberstalking",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Parent Charged After Anonymous App Messages to Soccer Coach", "Roster Cut Preceded 41 Texts From Unknown Number"],
        law: "cyberstalking",
        threshold: 9,
        spec: "Electronically communicated with {V} repeatedly from an anonymous account for the purpose of abusing, annoying, threatening, and harassing {V.him}.",
        ages: 36...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} coaches a youth select soccer team. Two days after {V} cut {D}'s child from the roster, {V} began receiving texts from an anonymous texting app: 41 over two weeks, mocking {V.his} coaching and naming {V.his} workplace. The app account was registered with {D}'s work email. {DL} says that mailbox is shared by a dozen coworkers.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "App Registration", "The account was registered with {D}'s work email."), E(.digital, 2, "Message Log", "41 messages over two weeks, many at night."), E(.document, 2, "Roster Cut", "{D}'s child was cut two days before the first message."), E(.statement, 2, "Coach", "{V} says the messages knew details only a parent would.")],
        defense: [E(.digital, 2, "Shared Mailbox", "The work email is accessible to about a dozen employees.")],
        role: "Detective with the cyber unit",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a detective with the cyber unit. I trace anonymous messages and accounts.\""), .direct("What did {V} report?", "\"41 texts over two weeks from an anonymous app, mocking {V}'s coaching and naming {V}'s workplace.\""), .direct("When did the messages start?", "\"Two days after {V} cut {D}'s child from the youth select roster.\""), .direct("How did you trace the account?", "\"The app account was registered with {D}'s work email address.\""), .direct("What did the message log show?", "\"41 messages, many sent late at night. They knew details only a parent would.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That the work mailbox is shared by about a dozen employees.\""), .direct("What did the app records show about where the account was used?", "\"The account was registered with {D}'s work email, and it was logged into from {D}'s phone at the practice field. Those two facts led us to {D}.\""), .cross("Did you find the messages came from {DL}'s phone?", "\"I found an account registered with the work email. I did not find the texts on {D}'s phone.\""), .cross("How many people could read the work mailbox?", "\"About a dozen employees. The IT administrator confirmed it.\""), .cross("Did you find a login from a library in another town?", "\"Yes. The same account was logged into from a library while {D} was at work.\""), .cross("Did the account also log in at the practice field?", "\"Yes. A login came from a phone at the practice field.\""), .cross("Whose phone was at the field?", "\"I could not tie it to a single person. Many parents stand at that field.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Company IT administrator",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role at the company?", "\"I am the IT administrator. I manage email accounts and mailboxes.\""), .direct("Who can access the work mailbox?", "\"About a dozen employees. It is a shared mailbox.\""), .direct("Can someone register an account with it?", "\"Yes. Anyone with access can use that address.\""), .direct("How is access tracked?", "\"Poorly. The mailbox does not log who reads each message.\""), .direct("Did you check the logs?", "\"I did. They do not identify a single person.\""), .direct("How would you describe {DL}?", "\"A normal employee. I have no reason to suspect {D}.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how the company's shared mailbox works.", "\"About a dozen employees can read and send from it. Anyone with the mailbox password can use it to register accounts on websites and apps.\""), .direct("Can the company tell who used the mailbox to register an account?", "\"Not reliably. The mailbox shows the address, but it does not show which person was sitting at the computer when an app registration email arrived.\""), .direct("How is the password shared among coworkers?", "\"It is written in a shared document and passed along when someone joins. Several people have used it for years, and it has never been changed.\""), .direct("Have you seen anyone else register accounts with that shared mailbox before?", "\"Yes. Coworkers have used it to sign up for software and apps for the office, and I have seen registration emails for services that no one remembers requesting.\""), .direct("Does the company log which employee reads messages sent to the shared mailbox?", "\"No. The system records that the mailbox was opened, but not which employee was sitting at the computer, so I cannot tell you who read or sent any particular message.\""), .cross("Was {DL} one of the dozen with access?", "\"Yes.\""), .cross("Did anyone else have a child on that team?", "\"I do not know.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} register the app?", "\"No.\""), .cross("Could you trace the login to a device?", "\"Not from our logs.\""), .cross("Who else used that mailbox that month?", "\"Many people.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used an anonymous account to harass the coach who cut a child.", "A shared mailbox and no proof of who typed."),
        allocution: "\"I was angry for my child. I'm sorry for all of it.\"",
        truths: ("The app account was logged into from {DL}'s phone at the practice field.", "The same account was logged into from a library in another town while {DL} was at work."),
        defendant: [.direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Hurt. My child worked hard and loved the team.\""), .direct("Did you send the texts?", "\"No. I never sent anonymous messages to {V}.\""), .direct("What about the work email?", "\"It is a shared mailbox. About a dozen coworkers can read and send from it.\""), .direct("Did you use that app?", "\"I have heard of it. I did not create an account.\""), .direct("What about the practice field?", "\"I go there to watch my child. Many parents do.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"I am sorry you were harassed. It was not me.\""), .direct("How did you feel when {V} cut your child from the roster?", "\"I was hurt and angry. My child worked hard, loved the team, and cried that night. I told {V} I disagreed, but I never sent anonymous messages.\""), .direct("What do you say about the account being logged into from your phone at the practice field?", "\"I was at the field because my child still practices there. I may have opened apps on my phone, but I did not log in to that account or type those messages.\""), .direct("What did you do when the detectives asked about the work email?", "\"I told them it is a shared mailbox used by about a dozen coworkers. I offered to let them check, because I had nothing to hide and I never typed those messages.\""), .cross("The account used your work email, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It is shared with others.\""), .cross("Your child was cut two days before the first text, correct?", "\"Yes. That is true.\""), .cross("The messages knew parent-level details, didn't they?", "\"They knew things many parents know.\""), .cross("Your phone logged in at the field, didn't it?", "\"I do not know what the logs say.\""), .cross("Many messages came at night, didn't they?", "\"So I understand.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} coaches a youth soccer team and received 41 anonymous texts over two weeks after cutting {D}'s child. The app account was registered with {D}'s work email. The State will show the registration and the log.", "A mailbox shared by a dozen coworkers can register any account. The company's IT administrator will tell you what the logs can and cannot show."),
        closings: ("A cut from the roster, then forty-one texts in two weeks, many at night, and an account registered with {D}'s work email and logged into from {D}'s phone at the practice field.", "A mailbox shared by a dozen coworkers and no proof of who typed a single message. The State has not proved {D} sent anything, and an angry parent is not the only person with access."),
        timeline: [(-16, "The roster cut."), (-14, "The first anonymous text."), (0, "The 41st message."), (25, "App records returned."), (35, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "App registration records.",
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .indifferent,
        impact: "I coached for the kids. I stepped away after this.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let shotsIntoHouseV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.shotsIntoHouse",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Gunshot Alert Pinpoints Four Shots Into Home After Bad Review", "Dark Pickup With Ladder Rack Seen Leaving"],
        law: "dischargingOccupied",
        threshold: 9,
        spec: "Willfully discharged a firearm into the occupied dwelling of {V}.",
        ages: 25...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 11:07 p.m. on {DATE}, a gunshot detection system flagged four shots near the home of {V}, who was inside with family. A traffic camera caught a dark pickup with a ladder rack leaving. Days earlier {V} had posted a bad review of {D}'s repair shop and {D} had replied, 'Keep talking. See what happens.' {DL} says {D.he} was working late at the shop.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Gunshot Detection", "Four shots at 11:07 p.m., within sixty yards of {V}'s home."), E(.video, 3, "Traffic Camera", "A dark pickup with a ladder rack passes ninety seconds later."), E(.document, 2, "Online Review Reply", "{DL}: 'Keep talking. See what happens.'"), E(.physical, 2, "Casings", "Four 9mm casings at the curb.")],
        defense: [E(.digital, 2, "Shop Alarm Log", "The alarm was disarmed at 10:20 p.m. and rearmed at 11:55 p.m.")],
        role: "Sheriff's detective",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as a sheriff's detective.", "\"I investigate shootings and threats. I collect casings, review camera video and detection data, and work with prosecutors to connect evidence to a person.\""), .direct("What did the gunshot detection system report?", "\"Four shots at 11:07 p.m., within sixty yards of {V}'s home. {V} was inside with family, and a bullet struck the wall of the home.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"Four 9mm casings at the curb and a bullet in the wall. The casings were bagged and sent to the lab for comparison.\""), .direct("What did the traffic camera show?", "\"A dark pickup with a ladder rack passing about ninety seconds after the shots. The plate was only partly visible, so I could not read the whole number.\""), .direct("Why did you look at {D}?", "\"Days before, {V} had posted a bad review of {D}'s repair shop, and {D} replied, Keep talking. See what happens. That reply was posted publicly.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the pistol?", "\"A pistol pawned two days later by a relative of {D} matched the four casings. The pawn shop records led us to that pistol.\""), .cross("Could you read the pickup's plate?", "\"Only part of it. The partial plate does not identify the pickup, and many dark pickups with ladder racks are common in the county.\""), .cross("Did you find the gun at {D}'s shop?", "\"No. We did not find a gun at the shop. We found it later through the pawn record, and we cannot say who fired it.\""), .cross("Did a former employee say anything about the pickup?", "\"Yes. A former employee later admitted to borrowing {D}'s pickup that night. That changes who may have been in the truck.\""), .cross("Where was {D} at 11:07?", "\"The shop alarm log shows it was disarmed at 10:20 and rearmed at 11:55, which is consistent with {D} being at the shop.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} fire a weapon?", "\"No. No witness saw who fired the shots. We have the detection data, the casings, the camera, and the reply, and no eyewitness.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Shop owner",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Explain to the jury how you know {D}.", "\"I own the shop next to {D}'s repair shop. We have been neighbors for years, and I see {D} at work nearly every day.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} at the shop that night?", "\"Yes. I saw the lights on and {D} working inside until late. I walked past around eleven and saw {D} at a bench.\""), .direct("What did you notice about {D}'s pickup?", "\"It was not in the lot when I walked by. I assumed someone had borrowed it, because {D} sometimes lends it to employees.\""), .direct("How does {D} handle disputes with customers?", "\"Usually by talking, and sometimes loudly. {D} gets annoyed at bad reviews but I have never seen {D} threaten anyone with violence.\""), .direct("What did you think when you heard about the shots?", "\"I was shocked. I could not believe {D} would do that. I told the deputies what I saw, and I told them {D} was at the shop.\""), .direct("Do other people have keys to the shop or the truck?", "\"Several former and current employees. The truck keys hang by the door, and anyone who works there knows where to find them.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} for the whole evening?", "\"No. I saw {D} around eleven. I cannot say where {D} was at 11:07 exactly, but the shop's alarm log is consistent with what I saw.\""), .cross("Could {D} have left the shop without your seeing?", "\"Yes. I was not watching the whole time. I cannot say that {D} did not step out, and I did not see anyone leave.\""), .cross("Did you see the former employee take the pickup?", "\"No. I only know what I heard afterward. I did not see anyone take the truck, and I did not see who drove it.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about the review to you?", "\"Yes. {D} complained about it. I told {D} to let it go, and {D} said something about not backing down.\""), .cross("Do you know about the pistol that was pawned?", "\"No. I only know what the deputies told me. I do not know anyone in {D}'s family who would do that.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shot into a home to scare a customer who posted a review.", "A mechanic at work, and a truck that is not unique."),
        allocution: "\"I was angry about the review. I never fired at anyone.\"",
        truths: ("A pistol pawned by {DL}'s brother two days later matched the four casings.", "A former employee later admitted he borrowed {DL}'s pickup that night."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about your repair shop.", "\"I own a repair shop and work long hours. I take pride in my work, and I try to answer every complaint, even when I disagree with it.\""), .direct("Why did you reply to {V}'s review with Keep talking?", "\"I was angry and I wrote it without thinking. It was a foolish thing to write, and I did not mean it as a threat of violence.\""), .direct("Where were you on the night of the shots?", "\"At the shop, working late on a job. The alarm log shows it was disarmed at 10:20 and rearmed at 11:55, and I stayed the whole time.\""), .direct("Did you fire a gun at {V}'s home?", "\"No. I did not. I never fired at anyone, and I would never put a family in danger over a review.\""), .direct("Who had access to your pickup that night?", "\"I did not lend it to anyone knowingly. A former employee later admitted to borrowing it that night. I did not know until the deputies told me.\""), .direct("What do you know about the pistol that was pawned?", "\"A relative of mine pawned a pistol two days later. I did not know about it, and I did not know it matched anything until the detectives told me.\""), .cross("Your reply said See what happens, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is what I wrote. I know how it reads, and I regret it a lot. I should have apologized instead of replying in anger.\""), .cross("Your truck matches the one on the camera, doesn't it?", "\"It is a dark pickup with a ladder rack, and so are many in the county. I was not driving it, so I cannot say who was.\""), .cross("The pistol that was pawned matches the casings, doesn't it?", "\"That is what the lab says. I did not own it, and I did not know it was used. I only learned about it afterward.\""), .cross("You could not prove you stayed at the shop all night, could you?", "\"The alarm log shows when I armed and disarmed the shop. It does not show every minute, but it shows I was there that evening.\""), .cross("You were angry at {V} that week, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was angry about the review. I am not proud of that, but I did not shoot at anyone, and I did not ask anyone to.\"")],
        openings: ("At 11:07 on a night in {DATE}, a gunshot detection system flagged four shots near the home of {V}, who was inside with family. Days earlier {V} had posted a bad review of {D}'s shop, and {D} had written back, Keep talking. See what happens.", "The defense will present a mechanic who was working late at the shop, a truck that was not unique, and a former employee who admitted borrowing it that night. An angry reply is not a shooting."),
        closings: ("Four shots, four casings at the curb, a dark pickup with a ladder rack, and a written warning in {D}'s own words. A pistol pawned two days later matched the casings, and the review was the motive.", "A mechanic working late with the shop alarm to prove it, a truck that is not unique, and a former employee who admitted borrowing it. An angry reply is not proof that {D} fired a gun."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{V} posts the review; {DL} replies."), (0, "11:07 p.m.: four shots."), (0, "11:09 p.m.: the pickup leaves."), (8, "Pistol recovered."), (15, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "A shot detection alert and a traffic camera.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant knowingly created a great risk of death to more than one person"],
        mitigating: ["No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "The bullet hit the wall above where my child sleeps.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "alibi"])

    static let occupiedHouseNightV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.occupiedHouseNight",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Intruder Steals Wallet and Tablet Through Garage Door While Family Sleeps", "Stolen Card Used at Gas Station Before Dawn"],
        law: "burglary1",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Broke and entered the occupied dwelling of {V} at night with intent to commit larceny therein, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 2 a.m. on {DATE}, someone came through an unlocked garage door into {V}'s kitchen while the family slept. A wallet and a tablet were taken. A porch camera recorded a hooded figure, and the wallet's card was used at a gas station at 2:40 a.m. The wallet was later found in {D}'s jacket. {DL} says {D.he} found it in a parking lot.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Gas Station Camera", "{D} buys fuel with the stolen card at 2:40 a.m."), E(.video, 2, "Porch Camera", "A hooded figure at the garage door at 1:55 a.m."), E(.physical, 3, "Wallet", "The stolen wallet in {D}'s jacket pocket.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found It", "{DL} says {D.he} found the wallet in a parking lot.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your home and your family for the jury.", "\"We live in a quiet neighborhood, and my family sleeps upstairs. I thought we were safe, and I never imagined someone would come into the kitchen at night.\""), .direct("What did you find when you woke up on {DATE}?", "\"The garage door was ajar and my wallet was gone from the kitchen. A tablet was missing too. I called the sheriff at about seven that morning.\""), .direct("What did the porch camera record?", "\"A hooded figure at the garage door at 1:55 a.m. The camera does not show a face, but it shows someone entering and leaving.\""), .direct("What happened with your wallet's card?", "\"It was used at a gas station at 2:40 a.m. The gas station camera shows {D} buying fuel with the stolen card.\""), .direct("How did the wallet come to be found?", "\"Deputies searched {D}'s jacket later and found my wallet inside it. It still had my cards and my identification.\""), .direct("How did this affect your family?", "\"We were frightened. We slept upstairs while someone walked through our kitchen. My children asked for a lock on every door, and we had a security system put in.\""), .cross("Did you see the intruder?", "\"No. We were asleep. I only know what the camera showed, and I cannot say who was in the hood.\""), .cross("Was the garage door locked?", "\"I thought it was, but it may have been unlocked. I do not remember checking that night, and I know that is part of what happened.\""), .cross("Can you say that {D} is the hooded figure?", "\"No. The hood hides the face. I can only say the wallet was later found with {D} and the card was used by {D}.\""), .cross("Did anyone else use the card?", "\"I do not know. A second camera shows someone handing the card to {D} in a lot a minute before the purchase, and I cannot say who that was.\""), .cross("Where did the phone data place {D} that night?", "\"Three houses away at 1:50 a.m. I do not know why {D} was there, but it is close to my home.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's roommate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell us how you know {D}.", "\"I am {D}'s roommate. We share an apartment, and I know when {D} comes and goes most nights, even though I do not keep track of every hour.\""), .direct("Was {D} home that night?", "\"No. {D} was out until after two. I heard {D} come in late, and {D} had a jacket with a wallet that {D} said was found.\""), .direct("What did {D} say about the wallet?", "\"{D} said {D} found it in a parking lot and wanted to return it. {D} showed me the ID and said {D} would figure out where it belonged.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D}?", "\"Quiet and usually honest. {D} pays rent on time and helps around the apartment. I was surprised to hear that {D} was accused of entering a home.\""), .direct("Did you see anything unusual about {D} that night?", "\"Only that {D} came home late and seemed tired. {D} did not seem scared or in a rush, and {D} did not mention a break-in.\""), .direct("What did you tell the deputies?", "\"I told them {D} was out that night and came home after two. I said I did not know where {D} had been, and I did not see a tablet.\""), .cross("Where was {D} that night?", "\"I do not know. {D} did not say where {D} was going, and I did not ask. I only know when {D} came home.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} with a tablet?", "\"No. I never saw a tablet. I only saw the wallet in the jacket, and I did not see any other items.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever bring home items that did not belong to {D}?", "\"Not that I noticed. I was surprised about the wallet, and I do not think {D} would break into a house.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you about the second person in the lot?", "\"No. {D} said nothing about anyone else. I only heard about that in the case, and I do not know who it was.\""), .cross("Could {D} have gone into the house without your knowing?", "\"Yes. I was asleep. I cannot say what {D} did between leaving and coming home, and I cannot rule it out.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered a sleeping home and used the stolen card.", "A finder of a lost wallet."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I know it was frightening.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone placed it three houses away at 1:50 a.m.", "A second camera shows another person handing the card to {DL} in the lot a minute before the purchase."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your night.", "\"I was out late. I walked through a neighborhood and ended up in a parking lot near a gas station. I did not break into any house.\""), .direct("How did you get the wallet?", "\"I found it in a parking lot. It was lying near the curb. I picked it up, looked inside, and kept it because I needed some money.\""), .direct("Why did you use the card at the gas station?", "\"I was low on gas and I did not have much cash. I used the card, and I know it was wrong, but I thought it was lost.\""), .direct("Did you enter anyone's home?", "\"No. I never entered any home. I did not go through any garage door, and I do not know who the hooded figure was.\""), .direct("Why did you keep the wallet in your jacket?", "\"I kept it for the ID so I could return it. I meant to turn it in, and I did not get around to it before deputies came.\""), .direct("What do you say about a second camera showing someone handing you the card?", "\"A person handed me the card in the lot, and I thought it was part of the same find. I did not think it was stolen.\""), .cross("The card was used at 2:40, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I used it to buy fuel. I did not use it for anything else, and I know that looks like what the thief would do.\""), .cross("Your phone was three houses from the home at 1:50, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was walking in that neighborhood. I did not go into the house, and I do not know why my phone was there at that time.\""), .cross("You kept the wallet in your jacket, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I kept it for the ID. I know that I should have turned it in, and I know the jury may not believe my story.\""), .cross("The wallet was taken from a kitchen, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the owner says. I did not take it from a kitchen. I found it in the lot, and I do not know how it got there.\""), .cross("You never called the owner or deputies, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I planned to, and I never did. I made bad choices that night, and I understand what the jury may think.\"")],
        openings: ("At 2 a.m. on {DATE}, someone came through an unlocked garage door into {V}'s kitchen while the family slept. A wallet and a tablet were taken, and the wallet's card was used at a gas station at 2:40 a.m. by {D}.", "The defense will present a finder of a lost wallet, a second camera showing a handoff in a parking lot, and a roommate who knows how {D} came home. Finding a wallet is not breaking into a home."),
        closings: ("A hooded figure at the garage door, a wallet taken from the kitchen, a card used at 2:40, and the wallet found in {D}'s jacket. {D} was three houses away at 1:50 a.m., and that is no coincidence.", "A wallet found in a lot, a card handed over by someone else on a second camera, and no one who saw {D} inside the home. The State has not proved {D} entered the house."),
        timeline: [(0, "1:55 a.m.: the porch camera."), (0, "2:40 a.m.: the card is used."), (0, "7 a.m.: {V} reports it."), (2, "Search of {DL}'s jacket.")],
        identified: "A card charge and a gas station camera.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I check the garage door three times every night.")

    static let mobileHomeSaleV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.mobileHomeSale",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Buyer Paid $14,200 Cash for Camper Trailer Hidden Lien Claimed", "Lender Repossesses Camper After Online Sale"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Obtained $14,200 from {V} by falsely representing that {D.he} owned a camper trailer free of liens and could sell it, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 35...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} paid {D} $14,200 in cash for a camper trailer advertised online with 'clear title in hand.' A lender repossessed it a month later over a $9,800 lien. Two earlier buyers had walked away after learning of the lien. {DL} says {D.he} co-owned the trailer and planned to pay off the lender with the sale.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Lien Record", "A lender's lien on the trailer for $9,800."), E(.digital, 3, "Online Ad", "The ad says 'clear title in hand.'"), E(.document, 2, "Bill of Sale", "Signed by {D} for $14,200 in cash.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Payoff Request", "A payoff request to the lender two days after the sale.")],
        role: "Buyer",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your search for a camper trailer for the jury.", "\"I wanted a camper trailer for my family. We had saved for a long time, and I searched online ads for weeks before I found one that looked right.\""), .direct("What did the online ad say?", "\"It said clear title in hand. That phrase was important to me, because I did not want to buy something with a lender's claim on it.\""), .direct("What did you do when you met {D}?", "\"I met {D}, looked at the trailer, and paid $14,200 in cash. {D} signed a bill of sale and told me the title was clear.\""), .direct("What happened a month later?", "\"A lender repossessed the trailer over a $9,800 lien. I received a notice and learned the title was not clear at all.\""), .direct("What did you learn about earlier buyers?", "\"Two earlier buyers had walked away after learning of the lien. I was not told that by {D}, and I would have walked away too.\""), .direct("What was the effect on you?", "\"I lost $14,200 and the trailer. We had planned a family trip, and I had to borrow money to cover our other bills.\""), .cross("Did you see the title before you paid?", "\"Only a copy. I did not ask to see the original. I trusted the ad and what {D} told me, and I know I should have checked.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to fix the lien afterward?", "\"I heard later that {D} sent a payoff request to the lender two days after the sale. I did not hear that from {D} at the time.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever pay anything toward the lien?", "\"The lender's records show {D} paid $2,000 toward it the week before the sale. I do not know about any other payments.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about co-owning the trailer?", "\"Yes. {D} said the trailer was shared with another owner. I did not think much about it at the time, and I should have asked more.\""), .cross("Did you check for liens before you bought?", "\"No. I did not run a check. I believed the ad, and I now know that was a mistake I made as a buyer.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Defendant's brother",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Walk us through how you are related to {D}.", "\"I am {D}'s sibling. We grew up together and we share some property, including the camper trailer that was sold.\""), .direct("How did you and {D} come to own the trailer?", "\"We bought it together a few years ago and shared the loan. We used it for family trips until money got tight.\""), .direct("What did {D} say about selling it?", "\"{D} said we should sell it and pay off the lender with the money. I agreed, and I thought {D} would handle the payoff.\""), .direct("Did {D} pay anything toward the lien before the sale?", "\"Yes. {D} paid $2,000 the week before the sale. I know because I saw the receipt, and I thought it was a good sign.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D} with money?", "\"Not careful with details, but not dishonest. {D} has always paid people back, even if it takes longer than promised.\""), .direct("What happened after the sale?", "\"{D} sent a payoff request to the lender, but the lender repossessed the trailer first. {D} was upset, and I was too.\""), .cross("Did you know about the lien?", "\"Yes. We both knew about it. It was part of why we wanted to sell, and we planned to use the sale to settle it.\""), .cross("Did you sign the bill of sale?", "\"No. I did not. {D} signed it alone. I think I should have signed, but I did not think about it at the time.\""), .cross("Did you tell buyers about the lien?", "\"I did not talk to any buyers. {D} handled that. I do not know what was said to the two who walked away.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell the buyer about the lien?", "\"I do not know. I was not there when {D} met the buyer. I only know what {D} told me afterward.\""), .cross("Did you get any of the $14,200?", "\"No. {D} kept it. I did not get a share, and I do not know how much went to the lender and how much did not.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} advertised a clear title that was not clear and took cash.", "A co-owner who meant to pay the lien off."),
        allocution: "\"I thought I could fix it before anyone lost out. I was wrong.\"",
        truths: ("Two earlier buyers had walked away after learning of the lien.", "The lender's records show {DL} paid $2,000 toward the lien the week before the sale."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about the camper trailer.", "\"I co-owned the trailer with a relative. We bought it together, and we had a loan on it. I wanted to sell it to pay down that loan.\""), .direct("Why did the ad say clear title in hand?", "\"That was poor wording. I meant the title would be clear once I paid off the lender, and I planned to use the sale money for that.\""), .direct("What did you tell buyers about the lien?", "\"I told some that the title would be clear, and I did not always explain the lien. Two earlier buyers walked away after they learned of it.\""), .direct("What did you do with the $14,200?", "\"I planned to pay the lender. I sent a payoff request two days after the sale, and I had paid $2,000 toward the lien the week before.\""), .direct("Why did the lender repossess the trailer?", "\"I did not pay the lien in time. I did not have the whole payoff when the cash came in, and I fell behind. I wish I had been honest.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Bad, more than anything. I never meant for the buyer to lose the trailer. I should have told the truth about the lien and waited to sell.\""), .cross("You said the title would be clear, didn't you?", "\"I said it would be. I know the ad said clear title in hand, and the title was not in my hand at the time.\""), .cross("You owned only half of the trailer, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I owned half, and a relative owned the other half. I should have had the relative sign the bill of sale as well.\""), .cross("The ad was misleading, wasn't it?", "\"It was poorly worded. I can see how a buyer would read it, and I should have said that a lien was still on it.\""), .cross("The lien was $9,800, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I knew about it. I planned to pay it off with the sale, but the lender took the trailer before I could.\""), .cross("You took cash and kept it, didn't you?", "\"I took cash for the trailer. I paid some to the lender, but not enough. I know it looks like I took advantage of the buyer.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} paid {D} $14,200 in cash for a camper trailer advertised online with clear title in hand. A month later, a lender repossessed it over a $9,800 lien, and two earlier buyers had already walked away after learning of it.", "The defense will present a co-owner who meant to pay off the lender with the sale, who had already paid $2,000 toward the lien, and who sent a payoff request two days later. A late payoff is not a plan to steal."),
        closings: ("An ad that said clear title in hand, a lien of $9,800 that {D} knew about, two buyers who walked away, and $14,200 in cash taken from {V}. The trailer was repossessed a month later.", "A co-owner who paid $2,000 toward the lien the week before, sent a payoff request two days after the sale, and meant to settle with the lender. The State has not proved that {D} meant to cheat."),
        timeline: [(-60, "Two buyers back out."), (0, "{V} pays $14,200."), (2, "Payoff request to the lender."), (30, "Repossession.")],
        identified: "{V} reported it after the repossession notice.",
        notDone: ["The brother's share was never checked in the records."],
        aggravating: ["The victim suffered serious financial loss"],
        mitigating: ["The defendant has made partial restitution"],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        impact: "That camper was our home while we looked for a house.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let fireworksStreetV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fireworksStreet",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Roman Candles Fired From Truck Bed at Gas Station Pumps", "Clerk Calls Deputies After Burst Near Pumps"],
        law: "disorderly",
        spec: "Disturbed the peace by setting off fireworks at a public gas station, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...45,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A gas station clerk called deputies on {DATE} at 11:30 p.m. after {D} fired roman candles from a truck bed near the pumps. A shell burst over the canopy. {DL} says {D.he} was running a send-off for a wedding party and the venue owner told {D.him} to use the lot.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Gas Station Camera", "{D} fires roman candles from a truck bed at the pumps."), E(.statement, 2, "Clerk", "The clerk says a shell burst over the canopy.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Send-Off", "{DL} says the venue owner told {D.him} where to light them.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a sheriff's deputy. I responded to the gas station call.\""), .direct("What did the clerk report at 11:30 p.m.?", "\"That {D} was firing roman candles from a truck bed near the pumps.\""), .direct("What happened with a shell?", "\"A shell burst over the canopy of the gas station, near fuel pumps.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"{D} standing in a truck bed firing roman candles toward the lot.\""), .direct("What did {DL} post?", "\"A countdown video with the words 'about to get loud.' I wouldn't want to guess beyond that, so that is my honest answer.\""), .direct("What did {DL} tell you?", "\"That a venue owner told {D} to use the lot for a wedding send-off.\""), .direct("What did the video you reviewed show about the shell that burst over the canopy?", "\"It shows {D} firing roman candles from the truck bed near the pumps, and one shell bursting directly above the canopy. Fuel pumps were running below, and the clerk called us.\""), .cross("Did anyone get hurt?", "\"No. Nobody was injured and the canopy was not damaged.\""), .cross("Was {DL} cooperative?", "\"Yes. {D} put away the fireworks and answered my questions.\""), .cross("Did the station owner give permission?", "\"No. The station had not agreed to anything.\""), .cross("Did the venue owner confirm hiring {DL}?", "\"Yes. The venue owner said {D} was hired to run a send-off.\""), .cross("How far were the pumps from the truck?", "\"Close. Perhaps thirty feet. It was too close for comfort.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} fired fireworks over a gas station.", "A send-off for a wedding party."),
        allocution: "\"I should have picked a safer place. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} posted a countdown video with 'about to get loud.'", "The venue owner had hired {DL} to run a send-off and pointed to that lot."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the gas station that night?", "\"I was running a send-off for a wedding party. The couple wanted fireworks as they left, and I was hired to run it.\""), .direct("Who told you to use that lot?", "\"The venue owner. I was pointed to that lot because it was open and near the road.\""), .direct("Did you think about the fuel pumps?", "\"I thought we were far enough. I should have asked the station. I see now I misjudged the distance.\""), .direct("What about the shell over the canopy?", "\"It flew higher than I expected and burst over the canopy. I never aimed it there.\""), .direct("Why did you post a countdown video?", "\"It was a fun post for friends before the send-off. It said about to get loud, and I meant the party.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"I am foolish. Nobody was hurt, but I should have thought harder about where I lit fireworks.\""), .direct("What did the countdown video you posted say about the send-off?", "\"I posted a countdown video with the caption about to get loud. It was for friends who wanted to watch the wedding send-off, and I did not think about fuel pumps.\""), .cross("You fired roman candles from a truck bed near fuel pumps, didn't you?", "\"Near the lot, yes. I misjudged how close we were.\""), .cross("You did not ask the station for permission, did you?", "\"No. I relied on the venue owner.\""), .cross("A shell burst over the station's canopy, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It did, and I am deeply sorry.\""), .cross("You posted about getting loud before you started, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, and I was excited.\""), .cross("It was 11:30 at night near gasoline, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I should have known better.\"")],
        openings: ("A gas station clerk called deputies at 11:30 p.m. after {D} fired roman candles from a truck bed near the pumps. A shell burst over the canopy. The State will show the camera and the clerk's account.", "A wedding send-off, a venue owner who pointed to the lot, and a countdown posted for friends. {D} says {D.he} had permission from the venue."),
        closings: ("Roman candles fired from a truck bed beside active fuel pumps at 11:30 at night, a shell bursting over the canopy, and a clerk who called deputies. The danger was obvious, and {D} chose to light them.", "A wedding send-off hired by the venue owner, a lot the owner pointed to, and a countdown posted for friends. The State has not proved that {D} meant to endanger anyone."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 p.m.: the send-off."), (0, "11:30 p.m.: roman candles."), (0, "11:45 p.m.: a deputy arrives.")],
        identified: "A gas station camera.",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let crosswalkHitRunV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.crosswalkHitRun",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Strikes Pedestrian at Dark Midblock Crossing and Flees", "Headlight Lens Fragments Lead to Pickup"],
        law: "hitAndRun",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Left the scene of a crash causing serious injury without stopping, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} was struck at a dark midblock crossing on {DATE} by a pickup that did not stop. Fragments of a headlight lens matched a pickup like {D}'s, and {D} had a headlight and fender repaired two days later. {DL} says the truck was at a friend's lot all evening.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Headlight Lens", "Fragments at the scene match a lens for {D}'s model of truck."), E(.document, 3, "Body Shop Order", "{D} had a headlight and fender repaired two days later."), E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Report", "A broken leg and cracked pelvis.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Parked Elsewhere", "{DL} says the truck was at a friend's lot.")],
        role: "Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a Highway Patrol trooper. I investigated the hit-and-run.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"{V} was struck at a dark midblock crossing by a pickup that did not stop.\""), .direct("What were {V}'s injuries?", "\"A broken leg and a cracked pelvis, per the medical report.\""), .direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"Fragments of a headlight lens matching a lens for {D}'s model of pickup.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That the truck was at a friend's lot all evening.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the repair of {D}'s truck after the crash?", "\"{D} had a headlight and fender repaired two days later. The shop owner told me {D} asked the shop to make it look old, and that detail is why I kept investigating {D}'s truck.\""), .cross("Did you see the truck at the crash scene?", "\"No. I found fragments of a lens. No one saw the truck itself.\""), .cross("Is that lens used on other trucks?", "\"Yes. It fits several pickups of that model and year.\""), .cross("Did anyone take a photo of {DL}'s truck before the crash?", "\"A county road crew photo from the week before shows the headlight already cracked.\""), .cross("Did the shop owner recall anything?", "\"Yes. The shop owner recalled {D} asking to make it look old.\""), .cross("Did {DL} talk to you?", "\"Yes. {D} said the truck was parked at a friend's lot all evening.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Friend who owns the lot",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {DL}?", "\"We have been friends for years. I own a small lot where {D} sometimes leaves the truck when {D} is out of town or busy.\""), .direct("Was {DL}'s truck at your lot on the evening of the crash?", "\"Yes. It was parked there when I arrived in the afternoon and it was still there when I locked up.\""), .direct("How can you be sure?", "\"I park my own car next to it and saw it every time I walked past. It had not moved that evening.\""), .direct("Did you notice damage on the truck?", "\"A cracked headlight on the front. It had been like that for some time, and I remember it from earlier weeks.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {DL}?", "\"Steady and decent. {D} would not hit someone and drive away, and I have never seen {D} act reckless.\""), .direct("Would you vouch for {DL}?", "\"Yes, without hesitation. I would not say any of this if I thought it was untrue.\""), .direct("What can you tell the jury about where the truck was the evening of the crash?", "\"It was parked in my lot when I arrived in the evening and it was still there when I left. I park my own vehicles beside it, so I would have noticed it moving.\""), .cross("Were you at the lot every minute that evening?", "\"No. I left for a while for dinner, so I cannot see every minute.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take the keys at any point?", "\"No. I did not see anyone take them.\""), .cross("Is your lot fenced or gated?", "\"No. Anyone could walk in.\""), .cross("Does {DL} have a spare key someone could use?", "\"I do not know. I have never asked.\""), .cross("Were you with {DL} that night?", "\"No. I was not with {D} at any point after the afternoon.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} hit a pedestrian and had the damage fixed.", "A truck that was parked elsewhere."),
        allocution: "\"I should have stopped.\"",
        truths: ("The shop owner recalled {DL} asking him to 'make it look old.'", "A county road crew photo from the week before shows the headlight already cracked."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where was your truck on the evening of the crash?", "\"Parked at a friend's lot the whole evening. I had left it there and was not behind the wheel that night.\""), .direct("Why did you take it to a body shop two days later?", "\"The headlight had been cracked for weeks and the fender was dented from an earlier bump. I finally decided to fix both.\""), .direct("Do you remember when the headlight cracked?", "\"Before the crash, a week or two earlier. A road crew photo from the week before even shows the crack.\""), .direct("What did you say to the shop owner?", "\"I asked them to make it match the rest of the truck. I might have said to make it look old, meaning not shiny and new.\""), .direct("What about the lens fragments at the scene?", "\"My model of pickup is very common around here. A lens like that fits many trucks, so a match does not point only to mine.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"Horrible. I am sorry for what happened. I wish I could help, but I was not the driver.\""), .direct("What do you say about the county crew's photo of your truck's headlight?", "\"A county road crew photographed my headlight a week earlier and it was already cracked. I repaired it because it was cracked, and not because of anything that happened at the crossing.\""), .cross("You repaired the truck just two days after the crash, didn't you?", "\"Yes, but I had been planning to for a while. I did not rush because of any crash.\""), .cross("You asked the shop to make it look old, didn't you?", "\"I said something like that, and I can see how it sounds. I meant matching the old finish.\""), .cross("The lens fragments match your model, don't they?", "\"They match a model many people drive. I did not hit anyone.\""), .cross("Your friend is the only one who says the truck was parked at the lot, correct?", "\"My friend is the one I know of who was there. I did not ask others.\""), .cross("You have no record showing the truck was parked all evening, do you?", "\"No record. I only have my friend's word.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} was struck at a dark midblock crossing by a pickup that did not stop. Headlight lens fragments matched {D}'s truck, and {D} had a headlight and fender repaired two days later. The State will show the lens and the shop order.", "A cracked headlight that county crews photographed a week earlier, and a friend who saw the truck parked all evening. {D} says it was never on that road."),
        closings: ("Lens fragments at the scene that match a headlight for {D}'s truck, a repair two days later, and a request to make the damage look old. A pedestrian lay in a dark crossing with a broken leg and cracked pelvis.", "A cracked headlight that county crews photographed a week earlier, and a friend who saw the truck parked all evening. The State has not proved that {D}'s truck struck {V}."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: the crash."), (0, "9:05 p.m.: a pickup leaves."), (2, "{DL}'s repair."), (5, "The lens match.")],
        identified: "Headlight lens fragments.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I use a walker, and I do not cross at night anymore.",
        doctrines: ["alibi"])

    static let vapeShopCounterV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.vapeShopCounter",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Smoke Shop Clerk Sold Oxycodone Pills Under the Counter, Deputies Say", "Informant Buy Recorded at Register"],
        law: "saleSchedII",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Sold oxycodone, a Schedule II controlled substance, to an undercover detective at a smoke shop on {DATE}.",
        ages: 22...34,
        victim: false,
        summary: "After an informant said the night clerk at a smoke shop sold pills, an undercover detective bought twenty oxycodone tablets for $200 on {DATE}. A camera recorded {D} pulling a bag from a register drawer. {DL} says the owner kept the bag there and told {D.him} to hand it to regulars.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Buy Video", "{D} takes a bag from the register drawer and hands it over."), E(.forensic, 3, "Lab Report", "Twenty oxycodone tablets."), E(.document, 2, "Marked Cash", "Marked bills recovered from the till.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Owner's Instructions", "{DL} says the owner kept the bag in the drawer.")],
        role: "Undercover detective",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as an undercover detective.", "\"I work narcotics undercover. I follow tips from informants, make controlled buys with marked cash, and record each transaction so that it can be reviewed later.\""), .direct("How did you come to buy pills at the smoke shop?", "\"An informant said the night clerk at the smoke shop was selling pills. I went in on {DATE} around 9:40 p.m. with $200 in marked bills.\""), .direct("What happened at the counter?", "\"I asked for pills. {D} pulled a bag from the register drawer, handed me twenty tablets, and took my $200 in marked cash.\""), .direct("What did the lab find?", "\"Twenty oxycodone tablets. The lab report confirms they were oxycodone, and the tablets matched the ones in the bag that {D} handed over.\""), .direct("What did you recover after the buy?", "\"We searched the shop at about ten and recovered the marked bills from the till. That tied the cash I paid to the register where {D} had been working.\""), .direct("What did you learn from the texts on {D}'s phone?", "\"One text said two more bottles of the blue ones tomorrow, bring cash. That suggested ongoing sales and not just a single transaction.\""), .cross("Who owns the shop?", "\"Someone other than {D}. {D} was the night clerk. The owner's fingerprints, not {D}'s, were on the bag we recovered from the drawer.\""), .cross("Did you see any other sale that night?", "\"No. I only saw the one I made. I cannot say how many other sales took place, and I did not watch the shop for days.\""), .cross("Where was the bag kept?", "\"In the register drawer. {D} says the owner kept it there and told {D} to hand it to regulars, and I cannot rule that out.\""), .cross("Did {D} seem nervous or unsure?", "\"No. {D} was calm and acted as if it were routine. That could mean {D} was used to it, or that {D} was following instructions.\""), .cross("Did you interview the owner?", "\"We spoke with the owner. The owner denied knowing about the bag, but the owner's fingerprints were on it, and we are still looking at the owner.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Other clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please tell us about your work at the shop.", "\"I work as a clerk on another shift. I work alongside {D} sometimes, and I know how the register and the drawer are used.\""), .direct("Did the owner keep things in the register drawer?", "\"Yes. A bag was kept there at times. The owner told us not to ask about it, and we were told to hand it to certain regulars.\""), .direct("What did the owner say about the bag?", "\"The owner said it was for regulars and that we should give it to them. The owner did not explain what was inside the bag.\""), .direct("What kind of clerk is {D}?", "\"Reliable and quiet. {D} follows instructions and does not complain. I have never seen {D} sell anything the owner did not approve.\""), .direct("Did you ever hand the bag to anyone?", "\"Once or twice, when the owner was not there. I did not open it, and I did not know what it was. I did what I was told.\""), .direct("What did you think when you heard about the case?", "\"I was scared. I realized I might have handed out something illegal. I told the deputies what I knew about the bag and the owner.\""), .cross("Did you ever sell from the bag yourself?", "\"No. I handed it over when I was told to. I did not keep any money, and I did not look at what was in the bag.\""), .cross("Did you ever see what was in the bag?", "\"No. I did not open it. I only knew it was kept in the drawer, and that the owner told us to hand it over.\""), .cross("Did the owner tell you it was a drug sale?", "\"No. The owner never said that. If I had known, I would have refused, but the owner kept it vague.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever say anything about selling pills?", "\"No. {D} never said anything like that to me. I did not hear {D} talk about pills at the shop.\""), .cross("Did the owner pay {D} extra for handing out the bag?", "\"I do not know. I was not told about any extra pay. I only know the owner kept the bag and gave instructions.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold oxycodone across the counter.", "A clerk following an owner's orders."),
        allocution: "\"I was using and I needed money. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("Texts on {DL}'s phone said, 'two more bottles of the blue ones tomorrow, bring cash.'", "The owner's fingerprints, not {DL}'s, were on the bag, and the owner later pleaded guilty in another county."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your job at the smoke shop?", "\"I work the night shift as a clerk. I ring up customers, restock shelves, and lock up. The owner sets the rules, and I follow them.\""), .direct("Why did you hand over a bag from the register?", "\"The owner kept it there and told me to hand it to regulars. I did what I was told and I did not look inside the bag.\""), .direct("What did you think was in the bag?", "\"I thought it was something the owner sold to regulars. I did not know it was oxycodone, and the owner never explained what was inside.\""), .direct("What did you do with the $200?", "\"I put it in the till. I did not keep any of it. I did what the owner told me, and I never took any cash for myself.\""), .direct("What about the texts on your phone?", "\"They were old messages from a friend about something else. I did not send them as part of selling anything at the shop.\""), .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"Mostly I feel used. I did what I was told, and now I am the one in court. I should have asked what was in that bag.\""), .cross("You pulled a bag from the register and handed it over, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know it looks bad, and I should have asked what was inside before handing anything over.\""), .cross("You took $200 in cash, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took the cash and put it in the till, as I was told. I did not think about whether it was a drug sale.\""), .cross("One text said bring cash, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It said that. It was about an old matter, and I did not connect it to the shop. I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("You did not call the owner when the detective came, did you?", "\"No. It never crossed my mind to call. I only did what I did every night, and I was shocked when deputies arrived.\""), .cross("The owner's prints were on the bag, but you handled it too, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I handled it when I gave it over. I did not know it mattered, and I did not wear gloves.\"")],
        openings: ("After an informant said the night clerk at a smoke shop sold pills, an undercover detective bought twenty oxycodone tablets for $200. A camera recorded {D} pulling a bag from the register drawer and handing it over.", "The defense will present a clerk who followed an owner's instructions, a bag the owner kept in the drawer, and fingerprints that belong to the owner. Handing over a bag as told is not the same as running a drug sale."),
        closings: ("A bag pulled from a register drawer, twenty oxycodone tablets, $200 in marked cash recovered from the till, and a text that said bring cash. The video shows {D} making the sale.", "A clerk who followed the owner's orders, a bag kept in the owner's drawer, and the owner's fingerprints on it. The State has not proved that {D} knew what was inside."),
        timeline: [(-20, "An informant names the clerk."), (0, "9:40 p.m.: the buy."), (0, "10 p.m.: search of the shop."), (30, "Lab confirms oxycodone.")],
        identified: "An informant's tip and a recorded buy.",
        mitigating: ["The defendant has a substance use disorder", "No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
