    static let pensionMotherV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pensionMother",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Meals Volunteer's Persistence Leads to Discovery of Mother's Death", "Social Security Deposits Continued for Ten Months After Death"],
        law: "concealingDeath",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Failed to notify law enforcement of the death of {V}, with the intent to conceal the death.",
        ages: 45...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A meals delivery volunteer was turned away at a door five times before deputies made a welfare check on {DATE}. They found {V}, 79, who lived with {D}, {V.his} adult child, dead in a sunroom recliner under blankets. The medical examiner estimated death ten months earlier from natural causes. In that time, $19,800 in Social Security deposits went into a joint account. {DL} says {D.he} could not accept the loss and was severely depressed.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Examiner", "Natural causes about ten months before discovery."), E(.document, 3, "Benefit Records", "$19,800 in Social Security deposits after the death."), E(.statement, 2, "Volunteer", "Turned away at the door five times.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Therapist Note", "{DL} was treated for depression that spring.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("How would you describe your job as a sheriff's deputy?", "\"I respond to welfare checks, accidents, and calls from neighbors. I check on people who cannot be reached, and I write reports on what I find.\""), .direct("Why were you called to the home on {DATE}?", "\"A meals delivery volunteer had been turned away at the door five times. The volunteer worried about {V}, and asked us to make a welfare check.\""), .direct("What did you find when you entered?", "\"I found {V}, age 79, in a sunroom recliner under blankets. {V} had been dead for a long time, and the room was closed up.\""), .direct("Who lived in the home?", "\"{V} lived with {D}, {V}'s adult child. {D} was home when we arrived, and {D} told me {V} was only sleeping.\""), .direct("What did the medical examiner say about the death?", "\"Natural causes about ten months before we found {V}. There were no signs of injury, and the examiner estimated the date from the condition of the remains.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the money?", "\"Records show $19,800 in Social Security deposits went into a joint account after {V}'s death. {D} had access to that account, and the money kept coming.\""), .cross("Did you see any sign that {V} was harmed?", "\"No. There was no sign of injury. The medical examiner found natural causes, and I did not see evidence that anyone hurt {V}.\""), .cross("Was there anything unusual about the room?", "\"The room was shut and the vents were covered. {D} said it was to keep it cool, and I have no way to prove otherwise.\""), .cross("Did {D} seem to understand that {V} was dead?", "\"{D} told me {V} was sleeping. {D} seemed confused and upset. I did not think {D} understood, and we called for help right away.\""), .cross("What did the calendar in {V}'s room show?", "\"A calendar marked each deposit date with a check. I cannot say who made the marks, and it could have been {V} or {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} resist the welfare check?", "\"No. {D} let us in after some hesitation. {D} did not try to hide the room, and {D} cooperated once we explained why we were there.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Treating therapist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What does your work as a therapist involve?", "\"I am a licensed therapist. I treat adults with depression, grief, and trauma, and I started treating {D} in the spring.\""), .direct("What was {D}'s condition when you first saw {D}?", "\"Severe depression. {D} was sleeping little, eating poorly, and withdrawn. Over time, {D} had a break from reality that I documented in my notes.\""), .direct("What did {D} believe about {V}?", "\"{D} believed {V} was only sleeping. {D} spoke about {V} as if {V} was alive, and {D} did not accept that {V} had died.\""), .direct("How was {D} functioning in daily life?", "\"Poorly. {D} could do routine tasks like paying bills, but {D} could not make sense of what happened. {D} avoided anyone who might tell {D} the truth.\""), .direct("What did your notes say about {D}'s grief?", "\"They said {D} was unable to accept the loss and was in a deep depression. I wrote that {D} showed signs of a break from reality.\""), .direct("Do you think {D} planned to keep the deposits?", "\"I do not believe {D} made a plan. {D} was not thinking clearly and was acting out of grief and illness, not out of a scheme.\""), .cross("Could {D} run the bank account?", "\"Routine tasks, yes. {D} could pay bills and shop, though {D} was not thinking clearly about what had happened to {V}.\""), .cross("Did {D} know that {V} had died?", "\"At some level, perhaps. But {D} could not accept it, and {D} told me {V} was sleeping. I cannot say what {D} knew in every moment.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever tell you about the deposits?", "\"Not in detail. {D} mentioned the account as shared, and I did not ask about the money. I was treating the depression.\""), .cross("Could {D} have asked for help sooner?", "\"In theory. But the illness made it hard for {D} to ask. I wish {D} had told someone, and I wish I had asked more.\""), .cross("Did you report the death or the deposits?", "\"No. I did not know about the death. {D} told me {V} was sleeping, and I only learned the truth when deputies made the welfare check.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} hid a parent's death and kept the deposits coming.", "Grief and illness, not a plan."),
        allocution: "\"I couldn't let go. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A calendar in {V}'s room marked each deposit date with a check.", "The therapist's notes show {DL} believed {V.he} was only sleeping."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your life with {V}.", "\"I lived with {V}, my parent, for most of my life. We shared a home, meals, and a bank account, and I cared for {V} in the last years.\""), .direct("What happened when {V} died?", "\"I found {V} in the sunroom and could not accept it. I told myself {V} was only sleeping, and I covered {V} with blankets.\""), .direct("Why did you turn away the meals volunteer?", "\"I was ashamed and afraid. I could not say what had happened, and I thought the volunteer would take {V} away if I opened the door.\""), .direct("Why did you cover the vents in the room?", "\"To keep it cool and keep {V} comfortable. I thought it would help, and I did not know what else to do.\""), .direct("What about the deposits into the account?", "\"We always shared that account. I used the money for bills the way we always had. I did not think about it as taking anything.\""), .direct("What treatment were you getting at that time?", "\"I started therapy that spring for depression. I could not sleep or eat, and I felt cut off from everyone. My therapist helped me, but I was very ill.\""), .cross("You did not call anyone when {V} died, did you?", "\"No. I did not call anyone. I did not believe it. I was in shock, and I know that sounds hard to understand.\""), .cross("You turned the volunteer away five times, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was ashamed. I knew I should have let someone in, and I did not know how to say what had happened.\""), .cross("You covered the vents, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wanted to keep the room cool. I did not realize what it meant, and I understand how it looks to the jury.\""), .cross("You kept receiving the deposits, didn't you?", "\"Yes. They went into our joint account. I did not use them for anything extravagant, but I know I should have reported the death.\""), .cross("You marked each deposit date on a calendar, didn't you?", "\"The calendar was in {V}'s room and had checks on it. I may have marked some dates, because we always tracked the deposits.\"")],
        openings: ("A meals volunteer was turned away at a door five times before deputies made a welfare check. They found {V}, 79, dead in a sunroom recliner for about ten months, while $19,800 in Social Security deposits kept going into a joint account shared with {D}.", "The defense will present a grieving, severely depressed child who could not accept a parent's death, and a therapist who treated {D} that spring. Grief and illness are not a scheme to collect money."),
        closings: ("Ten months, $19,800 in deposits, a volunteer turned away five times, and covered vents in a closed room. The deposits kept coming, and {D} never told anyone that {V} had died.", "A grieving, ill child who believed a parent was sleeping and did not make a plan to take money. The State has not proved that {D} meant to deceive anyone, and illness is not a scheme."),
        timeline: [(-300, "Estimated date of {V}'s death."), (-200, "{DL} starts therapy."), (0, "Welfare check; {V} is found."), (30, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "{D} lived in the home and received the deposits.",
        mitigating: ["The defendant suffered from a mental or physical condition that reduced culpability", "No prior criminal record"],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let giftCardSwapV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.giftCardSwap",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Customer Photographs Gift Card Numbers at Checkout Rack, Drains Balances", "Store Finds Nine Cards Redeemed Online"],
        law: "cardFraud",
        spec: "Obtained value from {V}, a retail store, by fraud involving gift cards, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A retail store learned on {DATE} that nine gift cards bought at its rack were drained before the buyers used them. A camera showed {D} photographing the backs of cards at the rack. The balances were redeemed online from {D}'s home address. {DL} says {D.he} was comparing card values for a gift.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Checkout Camera", "{D} photographs the backs of cards at the rack."), E(.digital, 3, "Redemption Log", "Nine cards redeemed online from {D}'s home address.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Comparing Values", "{DL} says {D.he} was comparing card values.")],
        role: "Store manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a store manager. I oversee the gift card rack and checkout.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"We learned that nine gift cards bought at our rack were drained before buyers used them.\""), .direct("What does the camera show?", "\"{D} photographing the backs of cards at the rack.\""), .direct("What does the redemption log show?", "\"Nine cards redeemed online from {D}'s home address.\""), .direct("What was found on {DL}'s phone?", "\"A spreadsheet of card numbers and PINs.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That {D} was comparing card values for a gift.\""), .direct("What did the redemption log show about where the cards were used?", "\"Nine cards were redeemed online from {D}'s home address. All nine had been bought at our rack and drained before any buyer used them.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the problem?", "\"Buyers came in to report that their gift cards were empty. Our records showed nine of them, and we pulled the camera and the redemption log to see what happened.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} redeem a card?", "\"No. I saw the camera at the rack and the online redemption log.\""), .cross("Could someone else have used {DL}'s home connection?", "\"Yes. The connection is shared with roommates.\""), .cross("Did a roommate admit anything?", "\"Later, yes. A roommate admitted redeeming cards on the shared connection.\""), .cross("Did {DL} buy gift cards too?", "\"I found no purchases by {D} at that rack.\""), .cross("Was the spreadsheet on {DL}'s phone?", "\"Yes. It listed card numbers and PINs.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} photographed card numbers and drained them.", "Someone who shared an address."),
        allocution: "\"I did it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A spreadsheet of card numbers and PINs was on {DL}'s phone.", "One of {DL}'s roommates later admitted redeeming the cards on the shared connection."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the gift card rack?", "\"I was shopping for a present and trying to decide which card to buy. I stood there a while comparing.\""), .direct("Why did you photograph the backs?", "\"To compare values and fine print later at home. It seemed easier than carrying them around.\""), .direct("What is the spreadsheet on your phone?", "\"A list of numbers I copied while comparing. I am not proud of how it looks, but I made it for my own reference.\""), .direct("Did you redeem any cards?", "\"No. I did not touch the balances on those cards. I never bought them.\""), .direct("Where did the online redemptions come from?", "\"From my home address, which is a shared connection with roommates who use the internet there too.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about the buyers who lost money?", "\"Terrible. Their gifts were drained, and I wish I had not been seen photographing cards.\""), .direct("What is the spreadsheet of card numbers and PINs on your phone?", "\"It is a list of cards I compared while shopping. A roommate later admitted redeeming the cards on our shared connection, and I did not know anything about that.\""), .cross("You photographed the backs of cards on camera, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I photographed several, and I know it looks suspicious.\""), .cross("Nine redemptions came from your home address, didn't they?", "\"Yes, from the address. Several people share that connection.\""), .cross("You had card numbers and PINs saved in a spreadsheet, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wrote them down while comparing.\""), .cross("You did not buy a single one of those cards, did you?", "\"No. I did not buy any.\""), .cross("A roommate had to admit redeeming the cards later, didn't one?", "\"Yes. A roommate did. I did not know at the time.\"")],
        openings: ("A store learned that nine gift cards bought at its rack were drained before the buyers used them. A camera showed {D} photographing the backs of cards at the rack, and the balances were redeemed online from {D}'s home address.", "The defense will present a shared home connection and a roommate who later admitted redeeming the cards. {D} says the photos were only for comparing card values, and a shared address does not prove who typed the numbers."),
