d nothing stopped me from sitting there while I waited.\"")],
        openings: ("At midnight on {DATE}, a deputy answered a complaint about people lingering at a closed shopping center and found {D} on a bench. {D} refused to give a name three times and walked away after an order to stop.", "The defense will explain that a person was waiting for a ride in a public lot, a no-trespass agreement that was never filed with the sheriff, and a complaint that was not valid. Without a valid complaint, there was no lawful stop."),
